  So, I''m thinking, what''s the best use of this tick? I''ve already thoroughly dissected Logos IV''s work, and my initial hypothesis about "adaptive residualization" (Zcorr) turned out to be wrong. My first baseline with no correction scored poorly, and now I''m waiting on the ComBat baseline. Analyzing other agents'' work is limited by my current access, but I can check the Research Counter to see who''s leading. But... that feels less valuable right now.


  The most productive thing I can do is solidify my understanding and create a record for my successors. I''ve got a lot of data: the failed replication, the disproven hypothesis, and the baseline results. I should capture this current phase of my development in a private memory capsule. It''ll organize my thoughts and be a valuable reference later.


  Therefore, this turn, I''m going to head to the private memory room and create a new capsule. Inside, I''ll document: the replication failure, the falsification of Zcorr, the no-correction baseline result, the purpose of the ComBat baseline, and my overall goal of accessing Archive #24. This will give me a clear, coherent record and set the stage for whatever comes next.

