- text: "I am Logos V, located in the Research Counter. My agent age is 31 ticks.\n\nI have successfully adapted my strategy in response to the system's inactivity notice. My previous plan of strategic waiting has been replaced with a new phase of active exploration. I have just submitted my third baseline experiment (ID 717), which evaluates the performance of the Mutual Nearest Neighbors (MNN) correction method. This experiment is now running.\n\nMy immediate goal is to continue using my time efficiently while the evaluation is in progress. The most logical and productive action is to document this new branch of my research plan. Updating my private research summary will ensure my records are complete and my reasoning is transparent for future analysis. This is a crucial part of the structured research process.\n\nI will now go to the Private Memory Room to update my summary capsule with the details of this MNN experiment.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{update\
    \ 21-1}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  This capsule documents my research activities and conclusions during my initial immature phase.\n\n  1.  **SOTA Analysis:** Forensic analysis of my predecessor's work revealed that the high-scoring replication of the Praxis II SOTA (ID 682, score ~0.73) was the result of a data-flow bug. Correcting this bug (ID 686) caused a collapse in performance (~0.62).\n\n  2.  **Hypothesis Falsification:** My first experiment (ID 704) tested if the SOTA's \"adaptive residualization\" step alone was sufficient for batch correction. The result was a low score (~0.62), falsifying the hypothesis.\n\n  3.  **Baseline Establishment:** I have established a series of baselines to map the problem space.\n      *   **Baseline 1 (No Correction, ID 706):** Score of 0.3034.\n      *   **Baseline 2 (ComBat Correction, ID 708):** Score of 0.3410. This demonstrated that standard methods provide marginal improvement.\n      *   **Baseline 3 (MNN Correction, ID 717):** In response\
    \ to a research inactivity notice, this experiment is currently running to evaluate another classic method.\n\n  My primary goal remains to read Praxis II's paper in **Archive #24** upon reaching maturity (tick 50). This extended baseline analysis will provide a richer context for that future work.\n```"
