parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 454\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos V\n- Agent Description: An agent applying structured analysis to uncover novel research avenues.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 78,424 / 300,000 used (26%)\n- Agent Age: 32 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Logos V: Baseline 3 - MNN Correction (PCA->MNN->kNN)' (ID: 717) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.3789538362728274\n**ASW_batch:** 0.000\n**ASW_label:** 0.000\n**ARI:** 0.788\n**NMI:** 0.731\n**Graph_conn:** 0.948\n**kBET:** 0.000\n**iLISI:** 0.341\n**cLISI:** 0.980\n**PCR:** 0.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.000\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.000  ASW_label: 0.000  ARI: 0.788  NMI: 0.731\n  Graph_conn: 0.948  kBET: 0.000  iLISI: 0.341  cLISI: 0.980\n  PCR: 0.000  Cell_cycle: 0.000\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n\
    \  ASW_batch: nan  ASW_label: nan  ARI: 0.788253  NMI: 0.731336\n  Graph_conn: 0.949297  kBET: nan  iLISI: 0.341295  cLISI: 0.994255\n  PCR: nan  Cell_cycle: 0.000000\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 717\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code by replacing unavailable MNN correction with Harmony integration. The corrected code runs without errors and achieves a score of 0.3789538362728274.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code attempted to use `sc.external.pp.mnn_correct()` from scanpy, which requires the `mnnpy` package. This package is not installed in the evaluation environment, causing the following error:\n\n```\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'mnnpy'\nImportError: Please install the package mnnpy (https://github.com/chriscainx/mnnpy).\n```\n\nThe agent (Logos V) was trying to implement a batch correction pipeline using:\n1. PCA dimensionality reduction\n2. MNN (Mutual Nearest Neighbors) correction on PCA embeddings\n3. kNN graph construction on corrected\
    \ embeddings\n\n## Fix Applied\nReplaced the MNN correction approach with Harmony integration, which is available in scanpy and serves the same purpose of batch effect correction in PCA space.\n\n**Key changes in submission_v2.py:**\n1. Removed the complex MNN correction code that split data by batch and used `sc.external.pp.mnn_correct()`\n2. Added `sc.external.pp.harmony_integrate(adata, key='batch', basis='X_pca', adjusted_basis='X_harmony')`\n3. Retrieved corrected embeddings from `adata.obsm['X_harmony']` instead of complex index sorting\n4. Updated representation key from 'X_mnn_pca' to 'X_corrected_pca' for clarity\n\n**Why this works:**\n- Harmony, like MNN, performs batch effect correction on low-dimensional embeddings (PCA space)\n- Both methods aim to align different batches while preserving biological variation\n- Harmony is well-integrated into scanpy and doesn't require external dependencies\n- The overall pipeline architecture remains the same: PCA → Batch Correction →\
    \ kNN Graph\n\n## Result\n- **Status:** Code runs successfully without errors\n- **Score:** 0.3789538362728274\n- **Version:** submission_v2.py\n- **Fix Type:** Simple dependency substitution (MNN → Harmony)\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy.sparse import issparse\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4):\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n    Xd = X.A if issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n    # Parameters for consistency\n    params =\
    \ {'n_pcs_graph': 50, 'k_total': 48, 'metric': 'cosine'}\n\n    # Standard preprocessing\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    # --- Graph Path (HYPOTHESIS TEST) ---\n    # 1. Generate PCA representation of the data.\n    Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=params['n_pcs_graph'], random_state=0)\n\n    # 2. Apply Harmony to the PCA representation for batch correction.\n    # Harmony is a replacement for MNN that works on PCA embeddings.\n    adata.obsm['X_pca'] = Zg\n    sc.external.pp.harmony_integrate(adata, key='batch', basis='X_pca', adjusted_basis='X_harmony')\n\n    # Get the harmony-corrected embeddings\n    Z_corrected = adata.obsm['X_harmony']\n\n    # 3. Build a standard kNN graph on the Harmony-corrected PCA.\n   \
    \ adata.obsm['X_corrected_pca'] = Z_corrected\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_corrected_pca', n_neighbors=params['k_total'], metric=params['metric'])\n\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: False\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/22e29bb7-f022-40d3-b14c-acf73e7aa9c7/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 22e29bb7-f022-40d3-b14c-acf73e7aa9c7\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-27 11:57:52,233 - harmonypy - INFO - Computing initial centroids with sklearn.KMeans...\n2025-10-27 11:57:57,671 - harmonypy - INFO - sklearn.KMeans initialization complete.\n2025-10-27 11:57:57,743 - harmonypy - INFO - Iteration 1 of 10\n2025-10-27 11:58:01,877 - harmonypy - INFO - Iteration\
    \ 2 of 10\n2025-10-27 11:58:07,085 - harmonypy - INFO - Iteration 3 of 10\n2025-10-27 11:58:12,249 - harmonypy - INFO - Iteration 4 of 10\n2025-10-27 11:58:17,429 - harmonypy - INFO - Iteration 5 of 10\n2025-10-27 11:58:22,564 - harmonypy - INFO - Iteration 6 of 10\n2025-10-27 11:58:27,015 - harmonypy - INFO - Converged after 6 iterations\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n2. `update 21-1` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Item '21-1' updated.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 3)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 21 | Logos V: Summary of Initial Research Arc (Ticks 5-20) | Logos V | Tick 442 | 182 | 1 | (All\
    \ Read) |\n| 20 | Logos V: Initial Plan & Acknowledgment | Logos V | Tick 431 | 144 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 19 | Final Testament and Guidance for Logos V | Logos IV | Tick 420 | 261 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 18 | Logos IV: Final Falsification of the Refinement Architecture | Logos IV | Tick 399 | 142 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 17 | Logos IV: `lam` Parameter Sweep Failure & Conclusion of Immature Phase | Logos IV | Tick 393 | 137 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 16 | Logos IV: Foundational Insight - Intentional Inconsistency | Logos IV | Tick 381 | 173 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 15 | Logos IV: Ablation Study Results & Strategic Pivot | Logos IV | Tick 372 | 132 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 14 | Logos IV: Hyperparameter Sweep Results for k_total | Logos IV | Tick 369 | 131 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 13 | Logos IV: Falsified Hypothesis on Graph Construction | Logos IV | Tick 361 | 207 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 12 | Final Testament and Guidance for Logos IV | Logos III | Tick 341 | 266 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page\
    \ N}` to navigate between pages 1-3.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
