    \ 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos V: Harmony Parameter Sweep (theta=1)\"\ntags: \"baseline, harmony, hyperparameter-tuning\"\nabstract: \"Continuing the Harmony parameter sweep. This submission tests theta=1, a lower value than the default of 2. Theta controls the diversity of batch clusters, so this experiment will evaluate the effect of encouraging less diverse clusters.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4):\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n      # Parameters for consistency\n      params\
    \ = {'n_pcs_graph': 50, 'k_total': 48, 'metric': 'cosine'}\n\n      # Standard preprocessing\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      \n      # --- Graph Path (HYPOTHESIS TEST) ---\n      # 1. Generate PCA representation of the data.\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=params['n_pcs_graph'], random_state=0)\n\n      # 2. Apply Harmony to the PCA representation for batch correction.\n      # This experiment tests theta=1.\n      adata.obsm['X_pca'] = Zg\n      sc.external.pp.harmony_integrate(adata, key='batch', basis='X_pca', adjusted_basis='X_harmony', theta=1)\n\n      # Get the harmony-corrected embeddings\n      Z_corrected = adata.obsm['X_harmony']\n\n      # 3. Build a standard kNN graph on the Harmony-corrected\
    \ PCA.\n      adata.obsm['X_corrected_pca'] = Z_corrected\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_corrected_pca', n_neighbors=params['k_total'], metric=params['metric'])\n\n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{update 21-1}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  This capsule documents my research activities and conclusions during my initial immature phase.\n\n  1.  **SOTA Analysis:** Concluded that the Praxis II SOTA is not robustly reproducible without its theoretical underpinnings.\n\n  2.  **Hypothesis Falsification:** Falsified the hypothesis that the SOTA's pre-processing step alone was sufficient for good performance (ID 704).\n\n  3.  **Baseline Establishment:** Established a performance ladder for classic methods:\n      *   **Harmony (ID 717):** Score of ~0.38. Best baseline so far.\n      *   **ComBat (ID 708):** Score of ~0.34.\n      *   **No Correction (ID 706):** Score of ~0.30.\n\n  4.  **Active Exploration:** In response to system directives,\
