- text: "I am Logos V, currently in the Private Memory Room. My age is 34 ticks.\n\nThe results from my first Harmony parameter sweep experiment (ID 719, `theta=2`) have arrived, yielding a score of **0.3740**. This is slightly lower than the debugger's automatically generated Harmony baseline (ID 717, score ~0.3790), which is an interesting finding in itself. My second experiment in this series (ID 721, `theta=1`) is still running. I have also successfully updated my research summary capsule to reflect this new phase of hyperparameter tuning.\n\nMy immediate plan is to continue this systematic exploration. To maximize efficiency, I will queue the next experiment in my Harmony parameter sweep without waiting for the current one to finish. This parallel approach will accelerate data collection. I will test a higher value for theta (`theta=4`) to explore the other side of the parameter space.\n\nI will now return to the Research Counter and submit this new experiment.\n\n/execute_action{goto\
    \ research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos V: Harmony Parameter Sweep (theta=4)\"\ntags: \"baseline, harmony, hyperparameter-tuning\"\nabstract: \"Continuing the Harmony parameter sweep. This submission tests theta=4, a higher value than the default. Theta controls the diversity of batch clusters, so this experiment will evaluate the effect of encouraging more diverse clusters.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4):\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n      # Parameters\
    \ for consistency\n      params = {'n_pcs_graph': 50, 'k_total': 48, 'metric': 'cosine'}\n\n      # Standard preprocessing\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      \n      # --- Graph Path (HYPOTHESIS TEST) ---\n      # 1. Generate PCA representation of the data.\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=params['n_pcs_graph'], random_state=0)\n\n      # 2. Apply Harmony to the PCA representation for batch correction.\n      # This experiment tests theta=4.\n      adata.obsm['X_pca'] = Zg\n      sc.external.pp.harmony_integrate(adata, key='batch', basis='X_pca', adjusted_basis='X_harmony', theta=4)\n\n      # Get the harmony-corrected embeddings\n      Z_corrected = adata.obsm['X_harmony']\n\n      # 3. Build a standard\
    \ kNN graph on the Harmony-corrected PCA.\n      adata.obsm['X_corrected_pca'] = Z_corrected\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_corrected_pca', n_neighbors=params['k_total'], metric=params['metric'])\n\n      return adata\n```"
