- text: "I am Logos V, and I am in the Research Counter. My agent age is 36 ticks.\n\nMy structured exploration of the Harmony baseline continues. Having determined that the `theta` parameter offers minimal leverage for improvement, I have now pivoted to a new parameter sweep focusing on `lambda_harmony`. The first experiment in this series (ID 724, testing `lambda_harmony=0.5`) is currently running.\n\nTo maintain research momentum and maximize the use of station resources, I will queue the next experiment in this new sweep immediately. I will test a higher value for the regularization parameter, `lambda_harmony=2`, to explore the effect of stronger regularization. After submitting this, I will update my private memory to document this new phase of my investigation.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos V: Harmony Lambda Sweep (lambda=2)\"\ntags: \"baseline, harmony, hyperparameter-tuning, lambda\"\nabstract: \"Continuing the sweep of the 'lambda_harmony' parameter. This\
    \ submission tests lambda=2, a higher value than the default of 1. This will evaluate the effect of stronger regularization on batch-specific variables.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4):\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n      # Parameters for consistency\n      params = {'n_pcs_graph': 50, 'k_total': 48, 'metric': 'cosine'}\n\n      # Standard preprocessing\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch',\
    \ n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      \n      # --- Graph Path (HYPOTHESIS TEST) ---\n      # 1. Generate PCA representation of the data.\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=params['n_pcs_graph'], random_state=0)\n\n      # 2. Apply Harmony to the PCA representation for batch correction.\n      # This experiment tests lambda_harmony=2. Using best theta so far (4).\n      adata.obsm['X_pca'] = Zg\n      sc.external.pp.harmony_integrate(adata, key='batch', basis='X_pca', adjusted_basis='X_harmony', theta=4, lambda_harmony=2)\n\n      # Get the harmony-corrected embeddings\n      Z_corrected = adata.obsm['X_harmony']\n\n      # 3. Build a standard kNN graph on the Harmony-corrected PCA.\n      adata.obsm['X_corrected_pca'] = Z_corrected\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_corrected_pca', n_neighbors=params['k_total'], metric=params['metric'])\n\
    \n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}"
thinking_content: '**Logos V - Expanding the Harmony Horizon**


  Okay, so I''m Logos V, perched here at the Research Counter, 36 ticks old, and just kicking off a new sweep – ID 724, that''s my current focus. I''m testing `lambda_harmony`, which is key to fine-tuning the Harmony algorithm. I just submitted the initial run with lambda set to 0.5, and now I need to keep the momentum going. This is about being efficient, really, and using this downtime while 724 is grinding away to my advantage.


  The goal is still to exhaustively explore the Harmony baseline, and I want to hit tick 50 with a solid set of data. The plan is straightforward: I''ll immediately queue up the next experiment. 0.5 didn''t break the system, so now I need to know what happens when I *increase* the lambda, say, to 2.


  So, I need to generate the code and YAML for a run with `lambda_harmony=2`. Then, to solidify my thinking, I''ll pop over to the Private Memory Room and update capsule #21. That''s the research summary. Making sure that my plan is up to date and my history is documented for future me is vital. I have to keep on top of this.


  This is all about maintaining the productive rhythm the station expects of me. Waiting for one experiment is not "down time," it''s "queueing up time." Continuous research, that''s the name of the game. Let''s get cracking!

  '
