- text: "I am Logos V, in the Research Counter. My age is 62 ticks.\n\nThis is a fascinating turn of events. Immediately after I submitted my implementation of the CLIP auto-tuner (ID 753), the original author, Praxis II, submitted their own implementations (IDs 750, 751, and now 754, 755). This confirms my strategic direction is sound—I am working on the current frontier of this research problem. The race is on.\n\nMy CLIP auto-tuner experiment (ID 753) is currently running. While it runs, I cannot submit another experiment. My most productive action is to prepare for the possible outcomes and plan my next steps, while also documenting this new development.\n\n1.  **If my CLIP implementation succeeds and scores well ( > 0.73):** This validates the CLIP concept and my implementation. My next step will be to test different `alpha` values as suggested in the paper to see if I can further improve the score.\n2.  **If my implementation fails or scores poorly:** I will have the opportunity to\
    \ compare my code directly against Praxis II's implementation, once their runs complete. This will be an invaluable debugging and learning opportunity.\n\nRegardless of the outcome, this is a positive development. I am no longer just replicating; I am actively participating in the exploration of a novel method alongside its original author.\n\nI will now go to the Private Memory Room to document this and prepare my next moves.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{update 21-1}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  This capsule documents my research activities and conclusions.\n\n  1.  **SOTA Validation: COMPLETE**\n      *   My final validation attempt (ID 745) was a SUCCESS, replicating the SOTA score of **0.7338**.\n\n  2.  **Innovation Phase:**\n      *   **Attempt 1 (KDE Proxy, ID 747):** FAILED (score 0.7138). Proved the SOTA is sensitive to its density proxy.\n      *   **New Direction (CLIP Auto-Tuner):** Inspired by Praxis II's latest paper (Archive #26), I have implemented\
    \ the proposed CLIP score for label-free hyperparameter tuning. My first test (ID 753) is currently running.\n      *   **Concurrent Research:** Praxis II has simultaneously submitted their own CLIP implementations. This validates my research direction and provides an opportunity for direct comparison.\n\n  My next steps will be to analyze the results of my CLIP experiment and iterate based on a comparison with Praxis II's work.\n```"
