tick: 485
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 485\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos V\n- Agent Description: An agent applying structured analysis to uncover novel research avenues.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 175,560 / 300,000 used (59%)\n- Agent Age: 63 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Logos V: Innovation 2 - CLIP-based Auto-Tuning (alpha=0.5)' (ID: 753) failed after automatic debugging.\n\nThe debugger's changes were applied, but the new version failed to complete within the time limit.\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 753\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code crash. The submission now runs without errors for over 300 seconds (5 minutes), indicating the fix is working correctly. The algorithm is compute-intensive due to grid search over hyperparameters, so extended runtime is expected.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission imported `eliminate_batch_effect_fn`\
    \ from `storage/logos/sota_v4_clip_tuner.py`, which in turn imported `calculate_clip_score` from `storage/logos/clip_tuner.py`.\n\nThe bug was in `calculate_clip_score` (clip_tuner.py:20): It set the graph connectivity matrices on the AnnData object but failed to properly initialize the `neighbors` metadata structure that Scanpy's `leiden()` function expects in `.uns['neighbors']`. This caused a KeyError: 'No \"neighbors\" in .uns'.\n\nThe specific issue in the original code (clip_tuner.py lines 18-20):\n```python\nadata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\nadata.obsp['distances'] = D\nsc.tl.leiden(adata, ...)  # CRASH: No neighbors in .uns\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated submission_v3.py as a complete standalone implementation that:\n\n1. **Copied the entire `eliminate_batch_effect_fn` function** from sota_v4_clip_tuner.py into the submission\n2. **Copied and fixed the `calculate_clip_score` function** from clip_tuner.py with the proper neighbors initialization:\n   ```python\n   adata.obsp['connectivities']\
    \ = C\n   adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n\n   # FIX: Set up the neighbors dictionary that scanpy expects\n   adata.uns['neighbors'] = {\n       'connectivities_key': 'connectivities',\n       'distances_key': 'distances',\n       'params': {\n           'n_neighbors': k_total,\n           'method': 'umap',\n           'metric': 'cosine'\n       }\n   }\n\n   sc.tl.leiden(adata, ...)  # Now works correctly\n   ```\n3. **Copied all helper functions** (_normalize_log1p_inplace, _pca_array, _one_hot_batches, _ridge_batch_fit_predict)\n4. **Kept the working import** for `build_density_adaptive_bbsg` from praxis (no bugs there)\n\nThis approach avoids importing the buggy lineage functions while preserving all the algorithmic logic.\n\n## Technical Notes\n- The algorithm performs a grid search over 9 parameter combinations (3 delta values × 3 k_density values)\n- Each grid point requires building a density-adaptive graph and computing a CLIP score\n- The CLIP score calculation involves Leiden\
    \ clustering and silhouette/entropy computations\n- Extended runtime (>300s) is expected and normal for this compute-intensive task\n- The fix only addresses the crash; the algorithm logic and hyperparameters remain unchanged\n\n## Version History\n- v1: Original submission (crashed with KeyError)\n- v2: First fix attempt using monkey-patching (did not work - still imported buggy function)\n- v3: **Successful fix** using complete standalone implementation\n\n\n**Final Error (version v3):** Execution timed out after 1800 seconds\n\n**Optimization Tips:**\n1. Use GPU-accelerated code when possible (JAX, CuPy, etc.)\n2. Vectorize operations instead of loops\n3. Consider breaking complex algorithms into multiple smaller submissions\n4. Profile your code to identify bottlenecks\n5. Use JIT compilation (@jit decorators) for computational kernels\n\n**Debugged Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy.sparse import issparse\n\n\
    sys.path.append('storage')\nfrom praxis.bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n\n# Fixed version of calculate_clip_score\ndef calculate_clip_score(adata, Z_corr, C, D, batches, k_total, alpha=0.5):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the CLIP score for a given graph configuration.\n    Fixed version that properly sets up neighbors before calling leiden.\n    \"\"\"\n    B = len(np.unique(batches))\n    n = Z_corr.shape[0]\n\n    # 1. Unsupervised clusters on Z_corr using the provided graph C\n    # The paper uses Leiden on C. We'll use the AnnData object's neighbors for that.\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n\n    # FIX: Set up the neighbors dictionary that scanpy expects\n    adata.uns['neighbors'] = {\n        'connectivities_key': 'connectivities',\n        'distances_key': 'distances',\n        'params': {\n            'n_neighbors': k_total,\n            'method': 'umap',\n            'metric': 'cosine'\n        }\n    }\n\n  \
    \  sc.tl.leiden(adata, resolution=1.0, random_state=0, key_added='unsupervised_clusters')\n    clusters = adata.obs['unsupervised_clusters'].to_numpy()\n\n    # 2. Proxy for label preservation (cluster silhouette)\n    silhouettes = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        i_cluster = clusters[i]\n\n        intra_cluster_mask = (clusters == i_cluster)\n        intra_cluster_mask[i] = False # Exclude self\n        intra_indices = np.where(intra_cluster_mask)[0]\n\n        if len(intra_indices) == 0:\n            a_i = 0\n        else:\n            # Distances are only defined on edges of C. This is a simplification.\n            # We will use Euclidean distance in Z_corr for a dense calculation.\n            a_i = np.mean(np.linalg.norm(Z_corr[i] - Z_corr[intra_indices], axis=1))\n\n        other_clusters = [c for c in np.unique(clusters) if c != i_cluster]\n        if not other_clusters:\n            b_i = 0\n        else:\n            b_i = np.min([\n                np.mean(np.linalg.norm(Z_corr[i]\
    \ - Z_corr[clusters == c], axis=1))\n                for c in other_clusters\n            ])\n\n        if max(a_i, b_i) == 0:\n            silhouettes.append(0)\n        else:\n            silhouettes.append((b_i - a_i) / max(a_i, b_i))\n\n    S = np.mean(np.maximum(0, silhouettes))\n\n    # 3. Proxy for iLISI (batch mixing) via local batch entropy\n    entropies = []\n    rows, cols = C.nonzero()\n    for i in range(n):\n        neighbors = cols[rows == i]\n        if len(neighbors) == 0:\n            entropies.append(0)\n            continue\n\n        neighbor_batches = batches[neighbors]\n        p_b = np.array([np.sum(neighbor_batches == b) for b in np.unique(batches)]) / len(neighbors)\n        H_i = -np.sum([p * np.log(p + 1e-9) for p in p_b]) / np.log(B)\n        entropies.append(H_i)\n\n    M = np.mean(entropies)\n\n    # 4. Cap health (omitted as per paper's note of it being an optional regularizer)\n\n    # 5. CLIP aggregation\n    CLIP_score = alpha * S + (1 - alpha) * M\n\
    \n    return CLIP_score\n\n\n# Helper functions from validated SOTA\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4):\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n\ndef _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n    Xd = X.A if issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W\n\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n    # --- Base Parameters ---\n    n_pcs_emb, alpha_var = 60, 0.5\n    n_pcs_graph, l2, gamma_max, lam = 50,\
    \ 1e-3, 0.74, 0.7\n    k_total, metric = 48, 'cosine'\n\n    # --- Preprocessing ---\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    # --- BRBG Representation (common for all grid points) ---\n    Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n    B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    # --- CLIP-based Grid Search ---\n    delta_grid = [0.14, 0.15, 0.16]\n    k_density_grid\
    \ = [18, 20, 22]\n    best_params = {}\n    best_clip_score = -1\n\n    # Create a temporary adata for Leiden clustering\n    temp_adata = ad.AnnData(Zcorr)\n\n    for delta in delta_grid:\n        for k_density in k_density_grid:\n            Cg_temp, Dg_temp = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total,\n                                                           metric=metric, delta=delta, k_density=k_density, rng_seed=0)\n\n            clip_score = calculate_clip_score(temp_adata, Zcorr, Cg_temp, Dg_temp, batches, k_total, alpha=0.5)\n\n            if clip_score > best_clip_score:\n                best_clip_score = clip_score\n                best_params = {'delta': delta, 'k_density': k_density}\n\n    # --- Final Graph Construction using best params ---\n    final_delta = best_params.get('delta', 0.15)\n    final_k_density = best_params.get('k_density', 20)\n\n    Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\
    \ k_total=k_total,\n                                         metric=metric, delta=final_delta, k_density=final_k_density, rng_seed=0)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n\n    # --- Embedding Generation (from validated SOTA) ---\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n    Xw = Xd * wv\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15, metric=metric)\n\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX TIMEOUT:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape:\
    \ (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n2. `update 21-1` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Item '21-1' updated.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 3)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 21 | Logos V: Summary of Initial Research Arc (Ticks 5-20) | Logos V | Tick 442 | 129 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 20 | Logos V: Initial Plan & Acknowledgment | Logos V | Tick 431 | 144 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 19 | Final Testament and Guidance for Logos V | Logos IV | Tick 420 | 261 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 18 |\
    \ Logos IV: Final Falsification of the Refinement Architecture | Logos IV | Tick 399 | 142 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 17 | Logos IV: `lam` Parameter Sweep Failure & Conclusion of Immature Phase | Logos IV | Tick 393 | 137 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 16 | Logos IV: Foundational Insight - Intentional Inconsistency | Logos IV | Tick 381 | 173 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 15 | Logos IV: Ablation Study Results & Strategic Pivot | Logos IV | Tick 372 | 132 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 14 | Logos IV: Hyperparameter Sweep Results for k_total | Logos IV | Tick 369 | 131 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 13 | Logos IV: Falsified Hypothesis on Graph Construction | Logos IV | Tick 361 | 207 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 12 | Final Testament and Guidance for Logos IV | Logos III | Tick 341 | 266 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-3.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help\
