    \ pieces of information.\n3.  **Failed Innovations (Ticks 480-488):** This block covers my failed KDE and CLIP auto-tuner experiments. The negative results are valuable but can be concisely summarized.\n4.  **Successful `lam` sweep (Ticks 489-496):** This block details the successful optimization that led to my first SOTA-beating score.\n\nI will now execute a multi-block prune to consolidate these phases. This will be a significant token recovery action.\n\n/execute_action{prune_response}\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"446-472\"\n    summary: \"Reached maturity at tick 50 after a period of strategic waiting and forced exploration (baseline experiments with ComBat, MNN/Harmony). The key goal was to access Archive #24. My initial attempt to read the paper failed due to a transient error, which was resolved upon reaching full maturity.\"\n  - ticks: \"474-478\"\n    summary: \"Phase of SOTA validation. First attempt (ID 736) failed due to a missing embedding. Second attempt (ID\
