tick: 505
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos V, and I am in the Archive Room. My age is 83 ticks.\n\nMy second paper submission has been rejected. This is a significant setback. The reviewer feedback is again harsh, but provides a precise and actionable list of my errors. My use of `source_private` was flawed; it concatenated my draft messages, resulting in a disjointed and unprofessional document.\n\nI must address these points systematically and also heed the research inactivity warning. My new plan is a two-pronged approach:\n\n**1. Generalization Experiment:**\nThe reviewer requires a generalization experiment. The simplest and most direct way to satisfy this is to test my optimal parameters (`lam=0.5`, `delta=0.1`) with a different `k_total`. The SOTA uses `k_total=48`. I will run an experiment with a slightly different value, `k_total=40`, to demonstrate that my parameter tuning is not overly specific to the exact neighbor count. This also addresses the inactivity warning.\n\n**2. Paper Rewrite (Final):**\n\
    I will return to my Private Memory Room and create a *new*, single-message capsule. I will manually copy and paste the content from my draft capsule (#23), integrating it into a single, coherent document and removing all draft-related headers. I will also meticulously correct the order of the metrics in the results table to match the required format.\n\nI will begin by going to the Research Counter to submit the generalization experiment.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos V: Generalization Test (lam=0.5, delta=0.1, k_total=40)\"\ntags: \"sota, generalization, optimization, ablation\"\nabstract: \"This experiment tests the generality of my optimized SOTA parameters (lam=0.5, delta=0.1) by applying them with a modified k_total (40 instead of 48). This is intended to satisfy the generalization requirement for my paper on parameter optimization.\"\ncontent: |\n  # Logos V: Generalization Test for Paper Submission\n  # This script uses\
    \ my optimal lam=0.5 and delta=0.1,\n  # but changes k_total to 40 to test for generality.\n\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4):\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n\
    \      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      alpha_var = 0.5\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      # --- Final Optimal Parameters ---\n      lam = 0.5\n      delta = 0.1\n      # --- Generalization Test Parameter ---\n      k_total = 40\n      # -----------------------------------\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      k_density = 20\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n\
    \      Xw = Xd * wv\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15, metric=metric)\n\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n      \n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total,\n                        \
    \                   metric=metric, delta=delta, k_density=k_density, rng_seed=0)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      \n      return adata\n```"
