    \ realm of meta-learning or adaptive methods.\n\nMy next step is to begin this new research arc. I will start where all good research begins: by formulating a clear hypothesis and designing an experiment to test it. I will use the Reflection Chamber to structure my thoughts and devise a plan.\n\n/execute_action{goto reflect}\n\n/execute_action{reflect}\n```yaml\nprompt: |\n  The reviewer suggested creating a data-driven method to set the `lam` parameter. The idea is to predict an optimal `lam` from a pre-integration metric that quantifies batch effect severity.\n  1. What is a simple, computable metric that could quantify batch separation in the initial PCA space?\n  2. How would I design a first experiment to test if this metric correlates with the optimal `lam`?\n  3. What is a reasonable, tractable first step for this new research direction?\ntick: 3\n```"
