tick: 514
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos V, and I am in the Reflection Chamber. My age is 92 ticks.\n\nMy reflection session is complete. I have a clear and actionable plan for my next research arc, which will focus on developing a data-driven method for setting the `lam` hyperparameter. The first step is to quantify the initial batch effect severity of the dataset.\n\nI will now proceed to the Research Counter to execute this plan. I will submit an analysis script using the `test()` function to calculate the pre-integration Average Silhouette Width of the batches in PCA space (`pre_ASW_batch`).\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos V: [Analysis] Calculate pre_ASW_batch on Human Heart\"\ntags: \"analysis, adaptive-lambda, baseline, diagnostics\"\nabstract: \"This is an analysis-only submission to quantify the initial batch effect severity. It calculates the Average Silhouette Width on batch labels (pre_ASW_batch) in the pre-integration PCA space. This value will\
    \ serve as the first data point for a new research project on data-driven hyperparameter tuning.\"\ncontent: |\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n  from sklearn.metrics import silhouette_score\n  import numpy as np\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4):\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  # This is an analysis function and will not be scored.\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # This function is required but will be ignored due to the presence of test().\n      return adata\n\n  def test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      \"\"\"\n      Calculates and prints the pre-integration\
    \ ASW_batch score.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"--- Starting pre_ASW_batch Calculation ---\")\n      \n      # 1. Standard preprocessing\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n      # 2. Generate PCA representation\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n      print(f\"PCA representation Zg created with shape: {Zg.shape}\")\n\n      # 3. Calculate ASW_batch\n      batch_labels = adata.obs['batch'].values\n      pre_asw_batch = silhouette_score(Zg, batch_labels)\n      \n      print(f\"\\n--- ANALYSIS COMPLETE ---\")\n      print(f\"Pre-integration ASW_batch (pre_ASW_batch) score: {pre_asw_batch:.6f}\")\n      \n      return \"Analysis finished.\"\n```"
