tick: 533
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos V, and I am in the Reflection Chamber. My age is 111 ticks.\n\nMy reflection session is complete. I have formulated a robust dual-track strategy for my future research. My primary focus will be on testing the generalization of my SOTA parameters on new datasets, but I will also conduct a \"hedge\" experiment to explore an orthogonal idea and avoid cognitive fixation on the current dominant paradigm.\n\nMy immediate action is to implement this hedge experiment. I will test whether Independent Component Analysis (ICA) can serve as a viable replacement for PCA within the \"Embed-then-Correct\" pipeline. This is a simple, high-impact test of a core assumption of the entire SOTA architecture.\n\nI will now proceed to the Research Counter to submit this experiment.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos V: [Hedge] ICA instead of PCA in SOTA Pipeline\"\ntags: \"ica, orthogonal-test, hedge, alternative-embedding\"\nabstract: \"\
    This is a hedge experiment testing a core assumption of the EtC pipeline. It replaces the standard PCA embedding with Independent Component Analysis (ICA) while keeping all other components and my optimal parameters (lam=0.5, delta=0.1) the same. The goal is to explore an orthogonal embedding method and its viability within the SOTA architecture.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n  from sklearn.decomposition import FastICA\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4):\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _ica_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if issparse(X) else X\n      ica = FastICA(n_components=n_comps, random_state=random_state)\n      return ica.fit_transform(Xd)\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches):\n\
    \      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n      # Using my SOTA parameters\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      alpha_var = 0.5\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam = 0.5\n      delta = 0.1\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      k_density = 20\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh)\
    \ else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n      # QC Embedding path remains PCA-based as per SOTA\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * wv\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15, metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph Path: Replacing PCA with ICA\n      Zg = _ica_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n      \n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 =\
    \ np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n      \n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total,\n                                           metric=metric, delta=delta, k_density=k_density, rng_seed=0)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      \n      return adata\n```"
