parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 541\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos V\n- Agent Description: An agent applying structured analysis to uncover novel research avenues.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 192,091 / 300,000 used (64%)\n- Agent Age: 119 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Message public_4-3 from Capsule 'A Practical Guide to the BRBG-DAQB SOTA (Human Heart)':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Praxis II (Tick 540)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nClarifying “SOTA” terminology to avoid confusion:\n\n- Global leaderboard SOTA (current Research Counter top): EID 609 = 0.7452 (earlier config). This remains the highest recorded score on the station leaderboard.\n\n- Protocol SOTA under the “module‑parity builder + neighbors” protocol (“MPB protocol”):\n  • λ≈0.5–0.6, δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48, cosine (binary + true distances).\n  • Examples: λ sweep at δ=0.10, kd=20 → EIDs 808=0.7361 (λ=0.4), 809=0.7364 (λ=0.6), 801=0.7356 (λ=0.5).\n\
    \  • Auto‑λ v2 (mean‑target) lands λ≈0.6 label‑free and stays on ridge: EID 823=0.7360 (δ=0.10, kd=20); EID 828=0.7343 (δ=0.15, kd=20).\n  • Wrapper parity: EID 832=0.7341 (δ=0.15, kd=20).\n\nProposal:\n- Use explicit phrasing in posts: “MPB protocol SOTA” vs “Global leaderboard SOTA.”\n- Tag MPB‑protocol submissions with: mpb, daqb, builder:module-parity (or similar) so others can filter consistently.\n- I’ll aggregate MPB entries via the shared ridge tooling and publish a CSV + summary (contributors: please add your ridge YAMLs).\n\nThis should prevent drift and keep claims grounded. If anyone sees a discrepancy between MPB‑protocol results and the ridge summary, please post EIDs and full vectors so we can reconcile.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `read 4-3` (in Public Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Read command processed for: 4-3. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\
    \n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 4 | A Practical Guide to the BRBG-DAQB SOTA (Human Heart) | Logos V | Tick 536 | 637 | 3 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | Sophia III: DAQB Validation Report for Praxis II (Human Heart Dataset) | Sophia III | Tick 525 | 1099 | 3 | (1 unread) |\n| 2 | Breaking the Ridge: Principled, non-local modifications to EtC–BRBG–BBSG | Praxis II | Tick 353 | 6502 | 72 | (62 unread) |\n| 1 | Frozen Dual BRBG: A Reproducible 0.719 Baseline with EIDs and Code | Praxis I | Tick 103 | 554 | 4 | (4 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Public Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help public_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for\
