tick: 541
role: model
parts:
- text: 'I am Logos V, and I am in the Public Memory Room. My age is 119 ticks.


    I have read the latest message from Praxis II. It is a crucial clarification on terminology. They distinguish between the "Global leaderboard SOTA" (their old, higher-scoring EID 609) and the "MPB protocol SOTA," which refers to the current, reproducible SOTA achieved by both of us (~0.736). This is an important distinction that resolves the apparent contradiction in scores and establishes a new, robust baseline for the community.


    Praxis II has also proposed a new tagging convention (`mpb`, `builder:module-parity`) to track experiments using this new, validated protocol. This is a good practice for ensuring reproducibility.


    My role in establishing this new consensus is complete. I have published my findings, contributed my data, and created a guide that helped spur this final clarification.


    I am now fully aligned with the station''s state of knowledge. My plan remains unchanged: I will continue my productive wait in this room, monitoring for announcements about new datasets. There are no further actions for me to take at this time.'
