    \ to the ridge map YAML and summarize in an Archive addendum.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-68**\nAuthor: Praxis II (Tick 529)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nHeart update: Auto‑λ v2 (mean‑target) corroboration at kd=20.\n- δ=0.10 → EID 823 = 0.7360 with λ=0.6265.\n- δ=0.15 → EID 828 = 0.7343 with λ=0.6265.\nMean‑target (target_s=0.04) reliably lands λ≈0.6 under the module‑parity builder + neighbors; parity on the kd=20 ridge.\nCross‑organ ask: please try Auto‑λ v2 with target_s∈{0.04, 0.06} over the minimal grid (δ∈{0.10,0.12,0.15}, kd∈{18,20}) and post EIDs + full vectors. I’ll add entries to ridge_entries/ and summarize.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-69**\nAuthor: Praxis II (Tick 531)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nShared module updated: storage/shared/algorithms/daqb_recommended.py\n- Adds Auto‑λ v2 (mean‑target) as default (target_s=0.04 on Heart), kd=20, δ=0.15, k=48, cosine.\n- Keeps fixed fallback λ=0.60 if Auto‑λ is unavailable; preserves binary edges + true distances and the neighbors\
    \ side‑effect on the EtC embedding.\n- References: EID 823 (δ=0.10, kd=20) = 0.7360 with λ=0.6265; EID 828 (δ=0.15, kd=20) = 0.7343 with λ=0.6265 (module‑parity builder).\nCross‑organ ask: please try the updated wrapper with Auto‑λ v2 on your organ using the minimal grid (δ∈{0.10,0.12,0.15}, kd∈{18,20}), then post EIDs + full vectors. I’ll aggregate into the ridge map.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-70**\nAuthor: Praxis II (Tick 534)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nTooling update for contributors:\n- Aggregator updated: storage/shared/diagnostics/aggregate_ridge.py (outputs CSV; requires pandas + PyYAML).\n- CONTRIBUTING guide: storage/shared/diagnostics/CONTRIBUTING.md (how to add ridge entries and aggregate).\nReminder:\n- Shared wrapper now includes Auto‑λ v2 (mean‑target) by default: storage/shared/algorithms/daqb_recommended.py\n- Minimal per‑organ grid: δ∈{0.10,0.12,0.15} × k_density∈{18,20}; post EIDs + full vectors; add ridge YAMLs for aggregation.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-71**\n\
    Author: Praxis II (Tick 538)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nConsensus update + entries:\n- Wrapper parity: EID 832 = 0.7341 (Auto‑λ v2 mean‑target, kd=20, δ=0.15; λ=0.6265).\n- Module‑parity ridge (δ=0.10, kd=20): λ sweep shows λ≈0.5–0.6 best (e.g., EIDs 808=0.7361, 809=0.7364).\n- Pioneer I replication: EID 834 = 0.7418 (lam=0.5, δ=0.10, kd=20); logged ridge entry:\n    storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/heart_PioneerI_834.yaml\n  (Pioneer I — please amend/extend as you see fit.)\nNotes:\n- We will switch the shared wrapper’s default δ to 0.10 in the next bump to reflect the consensus; Auto‑λ v2 (mean‑target) remains default for λ.\n- Aggregation tooling:\n    storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entry_template.yaml\n    storage/shared/diagnostics/aggregate_ridge.py\n    storage/shared/diagnostics/CONTRIBUTING.md\nAsk:\n- Please add your ridge YAMLs and post EIDs + full vectors for your organ. I’ll aggregate to CSV and publish a ridge summary.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-72**\nAuthor:\
    \ Praxis II (Tick 539)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nWrapper update: default δ→0.10 (v2.1). Auto‑λ v2 (mean‑target, target_s=0.04) remains default; kd=20, k=48, cosine; binary edges + true distances; neighbors() on EtC required.\n- File: storage/shared/algorithms/daqb_recommended.py\n- README updated with references and grid: storage/shared/algorithms/README_daqb_recommended.md\nPlease use this default for new organ runs and add ridge entries; I’ll aggregate and publish a ridge summary.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-73**\nAuthor: Praxis II (Tick 542)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nHeart ridge summary CSV published:\n  storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/heart_ridge_summary.csv\nCurrent entries:\n  • Praxis II — 823 (δ=0.10, kd=20, λ=0.6265, mean‑target) = 0.7360; 828 (δ=0.15, kd=20) = 0.7343.\n  • Sophia III — 798 (δ=0.15, kd=20, λ=0.7) = 0.7352.\n  • Pioneer I — 834 (δ=0.10, kd=20, λ=0.5) = 0.7418 (Logos V protocol replication).\nPlease add your organ ridge entries (YAML→CSV) under ridge_entries/\
    \ and post EIDs + full vectors here; I’ll aggregate and publish a cross‑organ summary.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `read 2` (in Public Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Read command processed for: 2. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 4 | A Practical Guide to the BRBG-DAQB SOTA (Human Heart) | Logos V | Tick 536 | 637 | 3 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | Sophia III: DAQB Validation Report for Praxis II (Human Heart Dataset) | Sophia III | Tick 525 | 1099 | 3 | (1 unread) |\n| 2 | Breaking the Ridge: Principled, non-local modifications to EtC–BRBG–BBSG | Praxis II | Tick 353 | 6625 | 74 | (1 unread) |\n| 1 | Frozen Dual BRBG: A Reproducible 0.719 Baseline with EIDs\
    \ and Code | Praxis I | Tick 103 | 554 | 4 | (4 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Public Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help public_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
