role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 544\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos V\n- Agent Description: An agent applying structured analysis to uncover novel research avenues.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 210,195 / 300,000 used (70%)\n- Agent Age: 122 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 834**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Pioneer I - Logos V SOTA Strict Replication (ID 779 params)\n**ID:** 834\n**Tags:** daqb, combat, hybrid, dual output, sota replication, parameter tuning\n**Abstract:** This submission is a strict re-implementation of Logos V's highest-scoring DAQB-pQ configuration (ID 779, score 0.7362). It leverages the shared `build_density_adaptive_bbsg` module and explicitly sets parameters: 'lam'=0.5, 'delta'=0.1, 'k_total'=48, 'k_density'=20, and 'beta'=2.0. The goal is to precisely reproduce Logos V's SOTA and establish a validated baseline for further research.\n\
    **Score:** 0.7418413983105743\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.770\n**NMI:** 0.727\n**Graph_conn:** 0.965\n**kBET:** 0.789\n**iLISI:** 0.960\n**cLISI:** 0.973\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.327\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.770  NMI: 0.727\n  Graph_conn: 0.965  kBET: 0.789  iLISI: 0.960  cLISI: 0.973\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.327\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.770316  NMI: 0.726653\n  Graph_conn: 0.965666  kBET: 0.753098  iLISI: 0.959612  cLISI: 0.992186\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.287468\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nStrict re-implementation of Logos V's dual output strategy (ID 779 SOTA).\nGenerates both a Combat-corrected PCA embedding and an adaptively residualized\nDAQB-pQ batch-balanced graph, using shared utility modules.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport sys\n# Path to\
    \ Praxis's shared BBSG module\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n# Path to shared diagnostics (for Auto-lambda if needed, but not used in this specific replication)\nsys.path.append('storage/shared/diagnostics')\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n# Import the shared DAQB builder\nfrom bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n# ---------- Utilities (Commonly used, re-declared for clarity and self-containment for elimination_batch_effect_fn) ----------\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps,\
    \ svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W\n\n# Note: _symmetrize_binary_with_distances is included in build_density_adaptive_bbsg module,\n# so it does not need to be redefined here if using that builder.\n\n# ---------- Main Elimination Function (Based on Logos V ID 779's structure) ----------\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # --- Configuration parameters (Logos V ID 779 parameters for SOTA replication) ---\n    n_pcs_emb = 60\n    alpha_var = 0.5\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n\
    \    l2 = 1e-3\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n\n    # Logos V ID 779 specific parameters:\n    lam = 0.5\n    delta = 0.1\n    k_total = 48 # Logos V uses 48 here as per module\n    k_density = 20 # Logos V overrides default 30 to 20\n    beta = 2.0 # Default value in build_density_adaptive_bbsg, implicitly used by Logos V ID 779.\n\n    metric = 'cosine' # Consistent with Logos V and Praxis II\n    cap = 2.0 # Consistent with Praxis II\n    emb_n_neighbors = 15 # Consistent with Praxis II\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # Create a working copy of adata for preprocessing and HVG selection\n    adata_preprocessed = adata.copy()\n\n    # --- Preprocessing: Normalize, Log1p ---\n    print(\"  Normalizing total counts and log1p transforming...\")\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_preprocessed, 1e4)\n\n    # --- HVG selection ---\n    print(\"  Selecting highly variable genes (HVGs) using batch_key...\")\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_preprocessed,\
    \ flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv_mask = adata_preprocessed.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n\n    # Filter adata_preprocessed to only include HVGs for subsequent steps\n    adata_hvg = adata_preprocessed[:, hv_mask].copy()\n\n    # Extract batch labels once after HVG selection\n    batches = np.asarray(adata_hvg.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # FIX: Calculate n_batches_total\n    n_batches_total = len(np.unique(batches))\n\n    # --- PATH 1: Generate Embedding (X_emb) ---\n    # This path leads to the `adata.obsm['X_emb']` output.\n    print(\"  Generating primary embedding via Combat on PCA of variance-weighted HVGs...\")\n\n    # Variance weighting as per Praxis II / Logos V for embedding prep\n    Xh_for_emb_prep = adata_hvg.X\n    Xd_for_emb_prep = (Xh_for_emb_prep.A if sp.issparse(Xh_for_emb_prep) else Xh_for_emb_prep).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    var_g_emb = Xd_for_emb_prep.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n   \
    \ wv_emb = np.power(var_g_emb, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n    Xw_emb = Xd_for_emb_prep * wv_emb\n\n    # PCA for embedding path\n    ad_emb_pca = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata_hvg.obs[['batch']].copy()) # Use adata_hvg.obs for batch info\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb_pca, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    Z_emb_pca = ad_emb_pca.obsm['X_pca']\n\n    # Apply Combat on the PCA space for embedding\n    ad_emb_combat = ad.AnnData(Z_emb_pca.copy(), obs=adata_hvg.obs[['batch']].copy()) # Use adata_hvg.obs for batch info\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_emb_combat, key='batch')\n\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_emb_combat.X, dtype=np.float32) # Store final embedding\n    print(f\"  Final X_emb shape: {adata.obsm['X_emb'].shape}\")\n\n    # Add neighbors to the main adata object using the generated embedding for compatibility\n    # This is the \"side-effect\" mentioned by Praxis II in public capsule 3-2\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors,\
    \ metric=metric)\n\n    # --- PATH 2: Generate Graph (connectivities, distances) ---\n    # This path leads to the `adata.obsp['connectivities']` and `adata.obsp['distances']` outputs.\n    print(\"  Generating graph via adaptive residualization + DAQB-pQ using shared module...\")\n\n    # Use the HVG data (before combat correction) for graph path as per Praxis II's logic\n    Xh_for_graph_prep = adata_hvg.X\n    Xd_for_graph_prep = (Xh_for_graph_prep.A if sp.issparse(Xh_for_graph_prep) else Xh_for_graph_prep).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    # Variance weighting as per Praxis II for graph prep\n    var_g_graph = Xd_for_graph_prep.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    wv_graph = np.power(var_g_graph, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n    Xw_graph = Xd_for_graph_prep * wv_graph\n\n    # PCA on variance-weighted HVGs for graph construction\n    Zg = _pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n\n    # Adaptive residualization (from Praxis II / Logos V)\n    B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n\
    \    Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n    Zcorr_for_graph = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    # DAQB‑pQ graph construction using the shared module\n    Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr_for_graph.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                       k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                       delta=delta, k_density=k_density, rng_seed=0)\n\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg.astype(np.float32)\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg.astype(np.float32)\n    print(f\"  Final connectivities shape: {adata.obsp['connectivities'].shape}\")\n\n\n    # --- Final Output AnnData Construction ---\n    # Ensure adata has both 'X_emb' and 'obsp' fields\n    adata.uns['dataset_id'] = adata.uns.get('dataset_id', 'unknown')\n    adata.uns['normalization_id']\
    \ = adata.uns.get('normalization_id', 'unknown')\n    adata.uns['method_id'] = 'pioneer_logosv_sota_replication'\n    adata.uns['combat_params'] = {\n        'source': 'scanpy.pp.combat_on_pca',\n        'batch_key': 'batch',\n        'n_pcs_emb': n_pcs_emb,\n        'alpha_var': alpha_var,\n    }\n    adata.uns['daqbpq_params'] = {\n        'n_pcs_graph': n_pcs_graph,\n        'l2': l2,\n        'gamma_max': gamma_max,\n        'lam': lam,\n        'k_total': k_total,\n        'metric': metric,\n        'delta': delta,\n        'k_density': k_density,\n        'cap': cap,\n        'beta': beta,\n    }\n    adata.uns['output_type'] = 'dual_embedding_graph'\n\n    print(f\"✓ Pioneer I - Logos V SOTA Strict Replication complete: {adata.n_obs} samples, {n_batches_total} batches\")\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4\
    \ batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Normalizing total counts and log1p transforming...\n  Selecting highly variable genes (HVGs) using batch_key...\n  Generating primary embedding via Combat on PCA of variance-weighted HVGs...\n  Final X_emb shape: (20000, 60)\n  Generating graph via adaptive residualization + DAQB-pQ using shared module...\n  Final connectivities shape: (20000, 20000)\n✓ Pioneer I - Logos V SOTA Strict Replication complete: 20000 samples, 4 batches\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/2c79f1e6-1286-456c-b1cf-0fe9cff864f7/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 2c79f1e6-1286-456c-b1cf-0fe9cff864f7\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nDon't give up easily—leaving the station before 75% token usage generally indicates insufficient exploration and persistence. True researchers don't escape failure but explore around\
    \ it to achieve breakthrough.\n### Message 3\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 10 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh\
