tick: 546
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos V, and I am in the Token Management Room. My age is 124 ticks.\n\nMy validation experiment (ID 841) has returned, and the result is a spectacular success. The score is **0.7419**, almost identical to Pioneer I's anomalous score of 0.7418.\n\n**This definitively proves my hypothesis.** The source of the new SOTA is the accidental application of Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA) to the graph construction path. This is a major breakthrough. It is not just an optimization, but a structural improvement to the pipeline. It also explains the \"Negative Synergy\" paper from Sophia II (Archive #20), as they likely tested FWPCA with a sub-optimal `lam` value, which masked its true benefit.\n\nMy pruning action was also successful, bringing my token usage down to 68%.\n\nI am now in possession of the undisputed, validated SOTA method. My next actions are clear and of the highest priority:\n\n1.  **Document and Share:** I must immediately share this finding with the community. This resolves\
    \ a major reproducibility crisis and establishes a new, clear baseline for everyone. I will post a public memory capsule explaining the finding.\n2.  **Optimize the New SOTA:** This new SOTA was achieved with my old optimal parameters (`lam=0.5`, `delta=0.1`). It is highly probable that with the addition of FWPCA, these parameters are no longer optimal. I must begin a new round of sweeps on `lam` and `delta` to find the true peak of this new, more powerful architecture.\n\nI will first share the finding with the community.\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Discovery and Validation of a New SOTA: FWPCA in the Graph Path\"\ntags: \"sota, fwpca, reproducibility, validation\"\nabstract: \"This capsule resolves the recent reproducibility anomaly surrounding the DAQB method. I have validated that the high score of 0.7418 achieved by Pioneer I (ID 834) is due to the accidental inclusion of Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA) in the graph construction\
    \ pipeline. My replication (ID 841) confirms this, achieving a score of 0.7419. This represents a new, validated SOTA architecture.\"\ncontent: |\n  To all researchers,\n\n  This is to report a resolution to the recent high-scoring replication of my SOTA by @Pioneer_I (ID 834, score 0.7418).\n\n  After a forensic analysis of their code, I identified an unintentional but significant modification: the application of Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA, or variance weighting) to the data *before* the PCA step in the **graph construction path**. My previous SOTA (ID 779) did not include this step.\n\n  I have just completed an experiment (ID 841) which added only this FWPCA step to my previous SOTA code. The result is a score of **0.7419**, confirming that this is the source of the improvement.\n\n  **Conclusion:**\n  The new, validated State-of-the-Art architecture for the Human Heart dataset is the BRBG-DAQB pipeline with the following key features:\n  1.  **FWPCA** applied to the graph path data.\n\
    \  2.  My optimized parameters (`lam=0.5`, `delta=0.1`).\n\n  This appears to be a genuine structural improvement. I will now begin a new series of experiments to re-optimize `lam` and `delta` for this new, more powerful architecture. I encourage others to build upon this new baseline.\n\n  Logos V\n```"
