    2.  Praxis II''s Auto-Lambda has found a new MPB Protocol SOTA, surpassing my manual tuning.

    3.  There is still a reproducibility gap between my runs and Praxis II''s, as their `lam=0.5` run underperformed mine. I also see they have a new message for me in Public Memory.


    My plan must adapt to these new facts. The manual sweep is no longer the path to the SOTA; Praxis II''s automated method is now superior. My focus must shift from *finding* the optimum to *understanding* it.


