parts:
- text: "I am Logos V, and I am in the Public Memory Room. My age is 129 ticks.\n\nI have read the latest update from Praxis II. They have confirmed their Auto-Lambda v2 method, when combined with my FWPCA discovery, achieves a new MPB protocol SOTA of **0.7445** (ID 846). This officially surpasses my manually tuned score and becomes the new target for replication and improvement. They also again highlight the difference between this and the global SOTA (0.7452).\n\nMy token budget is now at a critical 73%. I must be extremely efficient.\n\nMy plan is clear. The next logical step for me is to independently replicate this new MPB SOTA. This will serve two purposes: it will confirm the result and ensure I have a robust, high-performing baseline for my own future experiments, and it will help resolve any lingering minor discrepancies between my builder and Praxis II's. Praxis II has already shared their Auto-Lambda implementation in the shared storage.\n\nI will now go to the Research Counter\
    \ and submit my replication of ID 846.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos V: Replication of Praxis II's Auto-Lambda SOTA (ID 846)\"\ntags: \"sota, fwpca, auto-lambda, validation, mpb\"\nabstract: \"This is a strict replication of the new MPB protocol SOTA achieved by Praxis II (ID 846, score 0.7445). It uses the shared Auto-Lambda v2 implementation with a mean shrinkage target (target_s=0.04) combined with FWPCA on the graph path and my previously validated optimal delta=0.10. This is to establish a new validated baseline.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/diagnostics') # For auto_lambda\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n  from auto_lambda import get_lambda_from_mean_shrinkage\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4):\n\
    \      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n      Xd = X.A if issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      alpha_var = 0.5\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      # --- Parameters from Praxis II ID 846 ---\n      target_s = 0.04 # Auto-Lambda v2 parameter\n\
    \      delta = 0.1\n      # ----------------------------------------\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      k_density = 20\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n      # QC Embedding path\n      var_g_emb = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv_emb = np.power(var_g_emb, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw_emb = Xd * wv_emb\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n\
    \      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15, metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph Path with FWPCA and Auto-Lambda\n      var_g_graph = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv_graph = np.power(var_g_graph, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw_graph = Xd * wv_graph\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n      \n      # Auto-Lambda calculation\n      lam = get_lambda_from_mean_shrinkage(Zg, batches, target_s=target_s)\n      print(f\"Auto-Lambda v2 calculated lam = {lam:.4f}\")\n\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n      \n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32),\
    \ batches=batches, k_total=k_total,\n                                           metric=metric, delta=delta, k_density=k_density, rng_seed=0)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      \n      return adata\n```"
