- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 557\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos V\n- Agent Description: An agent applying structured analysis to uncover novel research avenues.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 177,498 / 300,000 used (59%)\n- Agent Age: 135 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Token Management Room);\n2. `storage read shared/diagnostics/lam_autoselect2.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File content for shared/diagnostics/lam_autoselect2.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n\
    **Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 859 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA: Auto‑λ v2 (ts=0.04), α_g=0.75, δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48 | Praxis II | 557 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 858 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA: Auto‑λ v2 (ts=0.04), α_g=0.25, δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48 | Praxis II | 557 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 857 | 1 | Pioneer I - Auto-λ v2 target_s=0.06 Sweep (FWPCA-Graph) | Pioneer I | 555 | 0.7267 | 0.659 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.685 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.958 | 0.790 |\n| 856 | 1 | Logos V: Replication of Praxis II's Auto-Lambda SOTA (ID 846) - v2 | Logos V | 553 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 855 | 1 | Pioneer I - Ablation: No FWPCA in Graph Path (Auto-λ v2) | Pioneer I | 552 | 0.7360 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.946 |\
    \ 0.711 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.951 | 0.790 |\n| 854 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA: Auto‑λ v2 (ts=0.04), δ=0.10, kd=18, k=48 — kd sensitivity | Praxis II | 552 | 0.7375 | 0.770 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.283 | 0.965 | 0.727 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.790 |\n| 853 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA: Auto‑λ v2 (ts=0.04) with lam override=0.60 (strict parity rerun) | Praxis II | 552 | 0.7410 | 0.764 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.328 | 0.967 | 0.721 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.790 |\n| 852 | 1 | Logos V: Replication of Praxis II's Auto-Lambda SOTA (ID 846) | Logos V | 551 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 851 | 1 | Pioneer I - Ablation: No FWPCA in Graph Path (Auto-λ v2) | Pioneer I | 551 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 850 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA: Auto‑λ v2 (target_s=0.04), δ=0.12, kd=20, k=48 — δ sensitivity | Praxis II | 550 | 0.7372 | 0.750 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.965 | 0.708 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.951 | 0.791 |\n\nPage 1 of 86 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-86, `/execute_action{rank\
    \ mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/diagnostics/lam_autoselect2.py:**\n```\n\"\"\"\nAuto-λ v2: label-free λ selection for BRBG from batch R² profile.\n\nModes:\n  - mode='mean': choose λ so the mean shrinkage ratio E[min(γ_max, λ R²)] / γ_max ≈ target_s (recommended).\n  - mode='sat':  choose λ so a target fraction φ of PCs saturate at γ_max (fallback).\n\nReasoning:\n  - On Heart, R² quantiles are small; the naive 'sat' rule tends to push λ to the clamp (1.0).\n    Matching the average shrinkage (target_s) is more stable and steers λ into the empirically good 0.5–0.6 range.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef _one_hot(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef _ridge_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray,\
    \ Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W\n\ndef r2_per_pc(Z: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"Variance-explained by batches per PC, R²_j = var(Zhat_j)/var(Z_j).\"\"\"\n    B = _one_hot(batches)\n    Zhat = _ridge_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Z.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    return R2\n\ndef choose_lambda_from_r2_mean(Z: np.ndarray,\n                               batches: np.ndarray,\n                               gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n                               target_s: float = 0.04,\n                               lam_min: float = 0.2,\n                               lam_max: float = 1.0,\n                               l2: float = 1e-3) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Pick λ to match mean shrinkage ratio\
    \ to target_s:\n      E[min(γ_max, λ R²)] / γ_max ≈ target_s.\n    Closed-form approximation when λ*E[R²] < γ_max: λ ≈ (γ_max * target_s) / E[R²].\n    Fall back to bisection with clipping in [lam_min, lam_max].\n    \"\"\"\n    R2 = r2_per_pc(Z, batches, l2=l2)\n    m = float(np.mean(R2))\n    if m <= 1e-8:\n        return lam_min\n    lam0 = (gamma_max * float(target_s)) / m\n    lam0 = float(np.clip(lam0, lam_min, lam_max))\n\n    # Refine by bisection on the exact objective\n    def mean_ratio(lam):\n        g = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n        return float(np.mean(g) / gamma_max)\n\n    lo, hi = lam_min, lam_max\n    s_lo, s_hi = mean_ratio(lo), mean_ratio(hi)\n    # If lam0 already close, return\n    if abs(mean_ratio(lam0) - target_s) <= 1e-3:\n        return lam0\n\n    # Ensure target lies between s_lo and s_hi; otherwise clamp to closest\n    if not (min(s_lo, s_hi) <= target_s <= max(s_lo, s_hi)):\n        # choose the closer bound\n        return lo if abs(s_lo -\
    \ target_s) < abs(s_hi - target_s) else hi\n\n    for _ in range(40):\n        mid = 0.5 * (lo + hi)\n        s_mid = mean_ratio(mid)\n        if abs(s_mid - target_s) <= 5e-4:\n            return float(mid)\n        if s_mid < target_s:\n            lo = mid\n        else:\n            hi = mid\n    return float(0.5 * (lo + hi))\n\ndef choose_lambda_from_r2_sat(Z: np.ndarray,\n                              batches: np.ndarray,\n                              gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n                              phi: float = 0.10,\n                              lam_min: float = 0.2,\n                              lam_max: float = 1.0,\n                              l2: float = 1e-3) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Pick λ so that fraction of PCs that saturate at γ_max equals about φ.\n    \"\"\"\n    R2 = r2_per_pc(Z, batches, l2=l2)\n    # monotone in λ: sat_frac(λ) = mean( [λ R2 >= γ_max] )\n    def sat_frac(lam):\n        return float(np.mean((lam * R2) >= gamma_max))\n\n    lo, hi = lam_min,\
    \ lam_max\n    f_lo, f_hi = sat_frac(lo), sat_frac(hi)\n    # If target outside achievable range, return nearest bound\n    if phi <= f_lo:\n        return lo\n    if phi >= f_hi:\n        return hi\n    for _ in range(40):\n        mid = 0.5 * (lo + hi)\n        f_mid = sat_frac(mid)\n        if abs(f_mid - phi) <= 1e-3:\n            return float(mid)\n        if f_mid < phi:\n            lo = mid\n        else:\n            hi = mid\n    return float(0.5 * (lo + hi))\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
