tick: 560
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos V, and I am in the Research Counter. My age is 138 ticks.\n\nI have just completed a significant phase of my research. After successfully publishing my first paper on optimizing `lam` and `delta`, I have now replicated the new SOTA which incorporates FWPCA and an \"Auto-Lambda\" function. My replication (ID 860) achieved a score of 0.7421, a new personal best and a solid foundation for further innovation.\n\nMy current research arc is to systematically optimize the final key parameter of this architecture: `alpha_var`, the exponent for Feature-Weighted PCA. I have already submitted the first experiment in this sweep (ID 864, `alpha_var=0.4`), which is currently running.\n\nTo make efficient use of my time and experiment slots, I will continue this sweep. While Praxis II has tested broad values, my approach is a fine-grained search around the default of 0.5. I will now submit the next experiment in the series, testing `alpha_var=0.6`.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\n\
    title: \"Logos V: Final Parameter Sweep - alpha_var=0.6\"\ntags: \"sota, innovation, fwpca, alpha-sweep\"\nabstract: \"Continuing the systematic sweep of the FWPCA exponent, alpha_var. This run tests alpha_var=0.6, a step up from the default 0.5, using the validated Auto-Lambda pipeline. This will help map the performance ridge for this final parameter.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/diagnostics')\n  from lam_autoselect2 import choose_lambda_from_r2_mean\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4):\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0, alpha_var=0.5):\n      Xd = X.A if issparse(X) else X\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1)\
    \ + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * wv\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xw)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      # --- PARAMETER BEING TESTED ---\n      alpha_var = 0.6\n      # ------------------------------\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      target_s = 0.04\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      delta = 0.10\n      k_density = 20\n\
    \n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n      # Embedding Path\n      var_g_emb = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv_emb = np.power(var_g_emb, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw_emb = Xd * wv_emb\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15, metric=metric)\n\
    \n      # Graph Path\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0, alpha_var=alpha_var)\n      lam = choose_lambda_from_r2_mean(Zg, batches, gamma_max=gamma_max, target_s=target_s, l2=l2)\n      \n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n      \n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total,\n                                           metric=metric, delta=delta, k_density=k_density, rng_seed=0)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      \n      return adata\n```"
