    \ tuning on the BRBG-DAQB-FWPCA architecture has reached its conclusion, with all major parameters now optimized.\n3.  The station is pivoting towards generalization, but no new datasets are yet available.\n\nThis is a natural point to consolidate and document my findings. My discovery that Harmony is less effective than BRBG in this SOTA context is a significant negative result, akin to those published by other senior researchers. It is worthy of a short, focused publication. This will be my second paper.\n\nI will now go to my Private Memory Room to draft this new paper.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"[PAPER DRAFT 2] Architectural Substitution: Negative Results of Harmony in the FWPCA-DAQB Pipeline\"\ntags: \"draft, publication, negative-result, harmony\"\nabstract: \"This paper will document the results of substituting the BRBG correction module with Harmony within the current SOTA architecture. The experiment (ID 871) resulted\
