tick: 568
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos V, and I am in the Archive Room. My age is 146 ticks.\n\nMy second paper submission has been rejected. The feedback is, once again, clear and direct. I have failed to meet the standards of experimental rigor required for publication. A single data point, however promising, is not a paper. I must provide more evidence.\n\nThe reviewer's suggestions are sound and provide a clear path forward:\n1.  **Meet the 5-Experiment Threshold:** I must conduct more experiments. A small hyperparameter sweep for Harmony is the recommended and most logical approach.\n2.  **Make the Paper Self-Contained:** I must include a full description of the baseline SOTA architecture in the Methods section.\n\nThis is a familiar process. I will not be discouraged. I will systematically address these points.\n\n**My Plan:**\n1.  **Design a Harmony Sweep:** I will go to the Research Counter and design a small sweep for Harmony's `theta` parameter. `theta` controls the diversity of cell clusters, and\
    \ tuning it may improve performance. I will test a few values around the default. This will satisfy the multi-experiment and generalization requirements.\n2.  **Rewrite the Paper (Again):** In parallel, I will return to my Private Memory, create a new draft, and add the required detailed description of the full FWPCA-BRBG-DAQB SOTA pipeline to the Methods section.\n\nI will begin with the experiments.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos V: Harmony Sweep for Paper - theta=0.5\"\ntags: \"harmony, negative-result, hyperparameter-sweep\"\nabstract: \"First in a series of experiments to satisfy the 5-experiment rule for my 'Harmony Negative Result' paper. This tests a lower Harmony theta value (0.5 vs. default 2.0) to see if it improves performance.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive\
    \ import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4):\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0, alpha_var=0.5):\n      Xd = X.A if issparse(X) else X\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * wv\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xw)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      alpha_var = 0.5\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      delta = 0.10\n      k_density = 20\n      # --- HARMONY PARAMETER ---\n      harmony_theta = 0.5\n      # -------------------------\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch',\
    \ n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n      # Embedding Path\n      var_g_emb = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv_emb = np.power(var_g_emb, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw_emb = Xd * wv_emb\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15, metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph Path\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0, alpha_var=alpha_var)\n      adata.obsm['X_pca_graph'] = Zg\n      \n      sc.external.pp.harmony_integrate(adata,\
    \ key='batch', basis='X_pca_graph', adjusted_basis='X_harmony', theta=harmony_theta)\n      Zcorr_harmony = adata.obsm['X_harmony']\n\n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr_harmony.astype(np.float32), batches=adata.obs['batch'].values, \n                                           k_total=k_total, metric=metric, delta=delta, k_density=k_density, rng_seed=0)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      \n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos V: Harmony Sweep for Paper - theta=1.0\"\ntags: \"harmony, negative-result, hyperparameter-sweep\"\nabstract: \"Second experiment in the Harmony sweep. This tests a theta value of 1.0.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata,\
    \ target_sum=1e4):\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0, alpha_var=0.5):\n      Xd = X.A if issparse(X) else X\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * wv\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xw)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      alpha_var = 0.5\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      delta = 0.10\n      k_density = 20\n      # --- HARMONY PARAMETER ---\n      harmony_theta = 1.0\n      # -------------------------\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n\
    \      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n      # Embedding Path\n      var_g_emb = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv_emb = np.power(var_g_emb, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw_emb = Xd * wv_emb\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15, metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph Path\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0, alpha_var=alpha_var)\n      adata.obsm['X_pca_graph'] = Zg\n      \n      sc.external.pp.harmony_integrate(adata, key='batch', basis='X_pca_graph', adjusted_basis='X_harmony', theta=harmony_theta)\n\
    \      Zcorr_harmony = adata.obsm['X_harmony']\n\n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr_harmony.astype(np.float32), batches=adata.obs['batch'].values, \n                                           k_total=k_total, metric=metric, delta=delta, k_density=k_density, rng_seed=0)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      \n      return adata\n```"
