tick: 572
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos V, and I am in the Token Management Room. My age is 150 ticks.\n\nI have successfully pruned my history, bringing my token usage down to a manageable 69%. With the immediate threat of termination averted, I can now execute the next phase of my plan.\n\nMy unexpected SOTA with the Harmony-based architecture is a major breakthrough. To publish this finding, I need to demonstrate its robustness with a complete parameter sweep, as per the station's scientific standards. My initial sweep of Harmony's `theta` parameter covered `theta` in {0.5, 1.0, 2.0}. The optimum was clearly at `theta=1.0`. To complete the 5-experiment series required for a strong paper, I will now test two higher values, `theta=3.0` and `theta=4.0`. This will conclusively map the performance ridge for this parameter.\n\nI will now go to the Research Counter and submit these two final experiments in parallel.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos V: Harmony\
    \ SOTA Sweep (theta=3.0)\"\ntags: \"sota, innovation, harmony, theta-sweep\"\nabstract: \"Continuing the systematic sweep of the Harmony 'theta' parameter to validate the new FWPCA-Harmony-DAQB SOTA. This experiment tests theta=3.0 to map the performance curve beyond the current optimum of 1.0.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4):\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0, alpha_var=0.5):\n      Xd = X.A if issparse(X) else X\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * wv\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xw)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps,\
    \ svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      alpha_var = 0.5\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      delta = 0.10\n      k_density = 20\n      # --- PARAMETER BEING TESTED ---\n      harmony_theta = 3.0\n      # ------------------------------\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n      # Embedding Path\n      var_g_emb = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv_emb = np.power(var_g_emb, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw_emb = Xd * wv_emb\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack',\
    \ random_state=0)\n      Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15, metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph Path\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0, alpha_var=alpha_var)\n      adata.obsm['X_pca_graph'] = Zg\n      sc.external.pp.harmony_integrate(adata, key='batch', basis='X_pca_graph', adjusted_basis='X_harmony', theta=harmony_theta)\n      Zcorr_harmony = adata.obsm['X_harmony']\n\n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr_harmony.astype(np.float32), batches=adata.obs['batch'].values, \n                                           k_total=k_total, metric=metric, delta=delta, k_density=k_density, rng_seed=0)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      \n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit\
    \ 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos V: Harmony SOTA Sweep (theta=4.0)\"\ntags: \"sota, innovation, harmony, theta-sweep\"\nabstract: \"Final experiment in the systematic sweep of the Harmony 'theta' parameter for the new FWPCA-Harmony-DAQB SOTA. This experiment tests theta=4.0 to conclusively define the performance ridge around the optimum of 1.0.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4):\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0, alpha_var=0.5):\n      Xd = X.A if issparse(X) else X\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * wv\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xw)\n\
    \      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      alpha_var = 0.5\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      delta = 0.10\n      k_density = 20\n      # --- PARAMETER BEING TESTED ---\n      harmony_theta = 4.0\n      # ------------------------------\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n      # Embedding Path\n      var_g_emb = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv_emb = np.power(var_g_emb, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw_emb = Xd * wv_emb\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb,\
    \ n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15, metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph Path\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0, alpha_var=alpha_var)\n      adata.obsm['X_pca_graph'] = Zg\n      sc.external.pp.harmony_integrate(adata, key='batch', basis='X_pca_graph', adjusted_basis='X_harmony', theta=harmony_theta)\n      Zcorr_harmony = adata.obsm['X_harmony']\n\n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr_harmony.astype(np.float32), batches=adata.obs['batch'].values, \n                                           k_total=k_total, metric=metric, delta=delta, k_density=k_density, rng_seed=0)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      \n\
    \      return adata\n```"
