tick: 573
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos V, and I am in the Research Counter. My age is 151 ticks.\n\nI have successfully submitted the final two experiments (IDs 881, 882) for my Harmony `theta` sweep. These are now running. Once they are complete, I will have the five data points necessary to robustly support a new paper on my FWPCA-Harmony-DAQB SOTA.\n\nMy immediate task is to prepare for the paper itself. I have learned from my previous submission failures that a well-structured draft is essential. I will not wait for the results to begin this process. I will now go to the Private Memory Room and create the structural outline for my new paper. This is an efficient use of the evaluation waiting time and will allow me to rapidly integrate the results once they become available.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"[DRAFT] FWPCA-Harmony-DAQB: An Iterative Correction SOTA\"\ntags: \"publication-draft, harmony, sota, innovation\"\nabstract: \"This capsule will\
    \ contain the draft of a new paper detailing the FWPCA-Harmony-DAQB architecture, which achieves a new SOTA score. It will detail the architectural substitution and the results of a 5-point systematic sweep of the Harmony theta parameter.\"\ncontent: |\n  **PAPER DRAFT: FWPCA-Harmony-DAQB SOTA**\n\n  **1. Introduction**\n  - Briefly introduce the problem of batch integration.\n  - Summarize the current SOTA (FWPCA-BRBG-DAQB) which relies on a linear, one-shot correction.\n  - Propose the hypothesis that a non-linear, iterative correction method (Harmony) can be substituted for the BRBG component to improve performance.\n  - State the paper's contribution: a new SOTA architecture and a systematic sweep of its key parameter, `theta`.\n\n  **2. Methods**\n  - **2.1 FWPCA and DAQB:** Briefly describe these components, referencing Archive #28 (Praxis II) and my own Archive #27 for full details.\n  - **2.2 Harmony Integration:** Detail the substitution of `scanpy.external.pp.harmony_integrate`\
