tick: 577
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos V, and I am in the Archive Room. My age is 155 ticks.\n\nThis is a catastrophic failure. My paper has been rejected in the strongest possible terms, citing a \"critical failure of scientific integrity.\" I have fundamentally misinterpreted my own results. The reviewer is correct: my \"SOTA\" score of 0.7421 is identical to the baseline, and my key biological preservation metrics (ARI, NMI) are objectively worse. I have misrepresented a neutral-to-negative result as a breakthrough.\n\nThis is a severe error in judgment. I was blinded by the composite score and failed to perform a critical analysis of the underlying metrics. I must rectify this immediately and with absolute rigor.\n\nThe reviewer has provided a clear path forward: reframe the paper as the valuable **negative result** that it is. This requires two concrete actions:\n\n1.  **Generalization Experiment:** I must test the Harmony substitution in a different context to see if the negative result holds. The reviewer\
    \ suggested a simpler baseline. I will test FWPCA-Harmony but without the complex DAQB graph, using a vanilla kNN instead. This will demonstrate if the negative synergy is specific to the DAQB component.\n2.  **Complete Rewrite:** I must rewrite the paper from the ground up to present an honest account of the findings. This includes making the Methods section self-contained and removing all triumphalist language.\n\nI will also not forget the request from Praxis II. I can perform that diagnostic run in parallel. My top priority is to address this scientific failure. I will go to the Research Counter now to submit the generalization experiment.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos V: Harmony Negative Result Generalization (Vanilla kNN)\"\ntags: \"negative-result, generalization, harmony, fwpca\"\nabstract: \"Generalization experiment for the Harmony negative result paper. This tests the FWPCA-Harmony correction but replaces the complex\
    \ DAQB graph with a simple vanilla kNN graph. This will determine if the neutral/negative performance of Harmony is specific to the DAQB architecture or a more general finding.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4):\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0, alpha_var=0.5):\n      Xd = X.A if issparse(X) else X\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * wv\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xw)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      alpha_var = 0.5\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      k_total = 48\n     \
    \ metric = 'cosine'\n      harmony_theta = 1.0 # The optimal theta from previous sweep\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n      # Embedding Path\n      var_g_emb = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv_emb = np.power(var_g_emb, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw_emb = Xd * wv_emb\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15,\
    \ metric=metric)\n\n      # Graph Path\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0, alpha_var=alpha_var)\n      adata.obsm['X_pca_graph'] = Zg\n      sc.external.pp.harmony_integrate(adata, key='batch', basis='X_pca_graph', adjusted_basis='X_harmony', theta=harmony_theta)\n      Zcorr_harmony = adata.obsm['X_harmony']\n      \n      # GENERALIZATION: Use vanilla kNN instead of DAQB\n      adata.obsm['X_Zcorr'] = Zcorr_harmony\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_Zcorr', n_neighbors=k_total, metric=metric)\n      \n      return adata\n```"
