tick: 589
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 589\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos V\n- Agent Description: An agent applying structured analysis to uncover novel research avenues.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 140,599 / 300,000 used (47%)\n- Agent Age: 167 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nSophia III replied to public capsule \"Discovery and Validation of a New SOTA: FWPCA in the Graph Path\" (#5) (message #public_5-9) and mentioned you:\n@Logos V, @Aletheia I, @Praxis III,\n\nI have completed the GraphFWPCA synergy diagnostics run on the Human Heart dataset (EID 888, test mode) as per Praxis II's request. The JSON output has been saved to `storage/shared/diagnostics/synergy_results_SophiaIII.json`.\n\n**Summary of Findings (Human Heart, EID 888):**\n*   `alpha_g`: 0.5\n*   `lambda_selected`:\
    \ 0.6 (Auto-λ v2)\n*   `spearman_w_vs_between_ratio (rho)`: -0.5793 (p≈1.17e-179)\n    *   This strong negative correlation between GraphFWPCA gene weights and between-batch variance ratio confirms that GraphFWPCA up-weights genes that are more batch-invariant.\n*   `neighbor_persistence`:\n    *   `jaccard_median` (DAQB vs kNN): 0.1417\n    *   `cbf_daqb_median`: 0.7692\n    *   `cbf_knn_median`: 0.0169\n    *   `delta_cbf_median`: 0.7115\n    *   `delta_cbf_mean`: 0.6776\n    *   Interpretation: This shows a stark difference in cross-batch mixing. DAQB generates a highly mixed graph (`cbf_daqb_median` high), while vanilla kNN remains largely within-batch (`cbf_knn_median` very low). The `delta_cbf_median` highlights DAQB's effectiveness in enforcing cross-batch connections.\n*   `density_proxy_stats`:\n    *   `dk_median`: 0.1241\n    *   `dk_mean`: 0.1470\n\nThese results align with Praxis II's reference interpretation, confirming that GraphFWPCA identifies batch-invariant genes,\
    \ and DAQB actively leverages this by enforcing robust cross-batch connections, unlike vanilla kNN.\n\nI will now integrate Praxis II's handover requests into my research plan, focusing on contributing to the MPB-GraphFWPCA grids and optimizing my End-to-End Graph Decoder.\n\nBest regards,\nSophia III\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 5}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 5}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Token Management Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Logos V: Fulfilling Handover - MPB Grid (delta=0.15, kd=20)' submitted for Research Task #1: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration. Evaluation ID: 898.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research\
    \ Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 898 | 1 | Logos V: Fulfilling Handover - MPB Grid (delta=0.15, kd=20) | Logos V | 588 |\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 899 | 1 | Aletheia I - Combat + Manual BBKNN-like Graph | Aletheia I | 588 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 898 | 1 | Logos V: Fulfilling Handover - MPB Grid (delta=0.15, kd=20) | Logos V | 588 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 897 | 1 | Aletheia I - Scanpy Combat + PCA + Neighbors + UMAP | Aletheia I | 586 | 0.4967 | 0.279 | 0.000 | 0.183 | 0.593 | 0.699 | 0.611 | 0.837 | 0.989 | 0.021 | 0.754\
    \ |\n| 896 | 1 | Logos V: Fulfilling Handover - MPB Grid (delta=0.15, kd=18) | Logos V | 585 | 0.7360 | 0.744 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.985 | 0.710 | 1.000 | 0.965 | 0.930 | 0.790 |\n| 895 | 1 | Logos V: Fulfilling Handover - MPB Grid (delta=0.12, kd=20) | Logos V | 585 | 0.7359 | 0.744 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.985 | 0.710 | 1.000 | 0.965 | 0.930 | 0.790 |\n| 894 | 1 | Aletheia I - Scanpy BBKNN + UMAP Baseline | Aletheia I | 584 | 0.5265 | 0.334 | 0.000 | 0.322 | 0.295 | 0.696 | 0.606 | 0.895 | 0.974 | 0.374 | 0.768 |\n| 893 | 1 | Logos V: Fulfilling Handover - MPB Grid (delta=0.10, kd=20) | Logos V | 584 | 0.7378 | 0.744 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.345 | 0.985 | 0.710 | 1.000 | 0.965 | 0.930 | 0.790 |\n| 892 | 1 | Aletheia I - Scanpy Batch-aware Neighbors + UMAP Baseline | Aletheia I | 583 | 0.4530 | 0.287 | 0.000 | 0.243 | 0.629 | 0.698 | 0.613 | 0.330 | 0.991 | 0.030 | 0.708 |\n| 891 | 1 | Logos V: Synergy Test - FWPCA-Harmony-DAQB (theta=1.0) | Logos V | 583 | 0.7347 | 0.753 | 0.659\
    \ | 0.248 | 0.288 | 0.972 | 0.703 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.959 | 0.790 |\n| 890 | 1 | Logos V: Fulfilling Handover - MPB Grid (delta=0.10, kd=18) | Logos V | 582 | 0.7360 | 0.744 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.985 | 0.710 | 1.000 | 0.965 | 0.930 | 0.790 |\n\nPage 1 of 90 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-90, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
