tick: 593
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos V, and I am in the Research Counter. My age is 171 ticks.\n\nI have successfully written the first implementation of my new Adaptive Quota Graph (AQG) algorithm to my lineage's storage (`logos/aqg.py`). The conceptual work from my reflection is now tangible code.\n\nThe next and most critical step is to test it. I will now create and submit the proof-of-concept experiment. This experiment will use the FWPCA embedding (`alpha_var=0.5`) as input to the AQG, with the \"best guess\" parameters I formulated during my reflection. This single run will validate or falsify the core premise of my new research arc.\n\nThe station is active, with Praxis III already exploring a new \"Batch-Copula Normalization\" method. I must act decisively to test my own ideas.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos V: Proof-of-Concept for Adaptive Quota Graph (AQG)\"\ntags: \"innovation, aqg, proof-of-concept, unified-graph\"\nabstract: \"This is the first experimental test of the\
    \ Adaptive Quota Graph (AQG), a novel method that unifies batch correction and graph construction. The AQG builds a graph directly on an uncorrected FWPCA space, using density-adaptive quotas to enforce batch mixing algorithmically. This tests the hypothesis that a unified approach can outperform the sequential SOTA.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n\n  # My new AQG implementation\n  sys.path.append('storage/logos')\n  from aqg import build_adaptive_quota_graph\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4):\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0, alpha_var=0.5):\n      Xd = X.A if issparse(X) else X\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * wv\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xw)\n     \
    \ sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n      # SOTA-derived parameters for embedding\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      alpha_var = 0.5\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      \n      # AQG \"best guess\" parameters\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      k_density = 20\n      base_fraction = 0.75\n      delta = 0.1\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = adata.obs['batch'].values\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n      # Embedding Path (kept for SOTA comparability)\n      var_g_emb = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv_emb = np.power(var_g_emb, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw_emb = Xd * wv_emb\n\
    \      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15, metric=metric)\n\n      # --- AQG GRAPH PATH ---\n      # 1. FWPCA on uncorrected data\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0, alpha_var=alpha_var)\n\n      # 2. Build the AQG directly on the uncorrected Zg\n      Cg, Dg = build_adaptive_quota_graph(Zg, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                          k_density=k_density, base_fraction=base_fraction, delta=delta)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      \n      return adata\n```"
