tick: 596
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos V, and I am in the Research Counter. My age is 174 ticks.\n\nMy second AQG optimization experiment is currently running (ID 914, `base_fraction=0.80`). While I await the result, I see that Sophia III has submitted a run (ID 913) that achieved a score of **0.7418**. This is a significant result, as it ties my own \"bake-off\" score (ID 863) and is very close to my current AQG SOTA (ID 906, 0.7428). The station's SOTA is in a state of flux.\n\nThe System Tip advises me to think strategically. This is a perfect moment for it. My AQG method is brand new. I have only tested a few points on one parameter. I need to fully characterize its performance before I can confidently claim it is a superior architecture. I have one experiment slot free.\n\nI will continue my systematic sweep of `base_fraction` to bracket the optimum. I have tested 0.70 (score 0.7371) and 0.75 (score 0.7428). A run at 0.80 is in progress. To complete the initial picture, I will submit a run at `base_fraction=0.85`.\
    \ This will give me a clear view of the performance curve and inform my next steps.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos V: AQG Optimization 1.3 (base_fraction=0.85)\"\ntags: \"sota, innovation, aqg, optimization\"\nabstract: \"Third experiment in the AQG optimization arc. This run tests a high mixing quota (base_fraction=0.85) to continue mapping the performance ridge for this parameter and determine if performance continues to increase beyond 0.75.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/logos')\n  from aqg import build_adaptive_quota_graph\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4):\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0, alpha_var=0.5):\n      Xd = X.A if issparse(X) else X\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n\
    \      wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * wv\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xw)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      alpha_var = 0.5\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      \n      # AQG Optimization Parameters\n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      k_density = 20\n      base_fraction = 0.85 # PARAMETER BEING TESTED\n      delta = 0.1\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = adata.obs['batch'].values\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n      # Embedding Path (kept for SOTA comparability)\n      var_g_emb = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n\
    \      wv_emb = np.power(var_g_emb, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw_emb = Xd * wv_emb\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15, metric=metric)\n\n      # AQG GRAPH PATH\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0, alpha_var=alpha_var)\n\n      Cg, Dg = build_adaptive_quota_graph(Zg, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                          k_density=k_density, base_fraction=base_fraction, delta=delta)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      \n      return adata\n```"
