    \n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/8c2447d5-fabd-4df3-a270-9f17891c2b70/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 8c2447d5-fabd-4df3-a270-9f17891c2b70\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nSophia III replied to public capsule \"Discovery and Validation of a New SOTA: FWPCA in the Graph Path\" (#5) (message #public_5-10) and mentioned you:\n@Logos V, @Praxis III, @Aletheia I,\n\nI have completed the full MPB-GraphFWPCA grid sweep on the Human Heart dataset as requested by Praxis II's handover. This sweep utilized the Auto-λ v2 (`target_mean_gamma=0.04`) for lambda selection and explored combinations of `delta` and `k_density`.\n\nThe optimal configuration found was **EID 913** (`delta=0.12`, `k_density=20`), which achieved a score of **0.7418**. The `lambda_selected` for all these runs was 0.6013. This result closely matches the MPB protocol SOTA.\n\nHere is a summary of the full grid:\n\
    \n**Summary Table: MPB-GraphFWPCA Grid (alpha_g=0.5, target_s=0.04)**\n| EID | k-density | delta | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET | lambda_selected |\n|-----|-----------|-------|-------|-----|-----------|-----------|------------|------------|-----|-----|-------|-------|------|-----------------|\n| 900 | 18        | 0.10  | 0.7354| 0.739| 0.659     | 0.248     | 0.327      | 0.985      | 0.707| 1.000| 0.965  | 0.930 | 0.792| 0.6013          |\n| 903 | 18        | 0.12  | 0.7367| 0.744| 0.659     | 0.248     | 0.332      | 0.986      | 0.709| 1.000| 0.965  | 0.935 | 0.789| 0.6013          |\n| 907 | 18        | 0.15  | 0.7359| 0.743| 0.659     | 0.248     | 0.327      | 0.986      | 0.709| 1.000| 0.964  | 0.932 | 0.790| 0.6013          |\n| 908 | 20        | 0.10  | 0.7361| 0.744| 0.659     | 0.248     | 0.327      | 0.986      | 0.710| 1.000| 0.965  | 0.931 | 0.790| 0.6013          |\n| **913** | **20**    | **0.12**| **0.7418**|\
    \ 0.743| 0.659     | 0.248     | 0.383      | 0.986      | 0.708| 1.000| 0.965  | 0.935 | 0.790| 0.6013          |\n| 915 | 20        | 0.15  | 0.7358| 0.743| 0.659     | 0.248     | 0.327      | 0.986      | 0.707| 1.000| 0.964  | 0.932 | 0.790| 0.6013          |\n\nThe detailed YAML parameters and full metric vector for EID 913 have been mirrored to `storage/shared/diagnostics/ridge_entries/heart_SophiaIII_913.yaml`.\n\nThis systematic sweep helps confirm the robustness of the MPB-GraphFWPCA architecture across these parameters. I will now reflect on incorporating these insights into my ongoing End-to-End Graph Decoder development and consider new research directions.\n\nBest regards,\nSophia III\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 5}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 5}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract,\
    \ content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Logos V: AQG Optimization 2.2 (delta=0.15)' submitted for Research Task #1: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration. Evaluation ID: 925.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 925 | 1 | Logos V: AQG Optimization 2.2 (delta=0.15) | Logos V | 598 |\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 927 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA (power γ): p=1.5, mean‑target 0.04, δ=0.11, kd=20, k=48 (import fix) | Praxis III | 598 | running |  |  |  |\
    \  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 926 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA (power γ): p=1.5, mean‑target 0.04, δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48 (import fix) | Praxis III | 598 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 925 | 1 | Logos V: AQG Optimization 2.2 (delta=0.15) | Logos V | 598 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 924 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA (power γ): p=1.5, mean‑target 0.04, δ=0.11, kd=20, k=48 | Praxis III | 597 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 923 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA (power γ): p=1.5, mean‑target 0.04, δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48 | Praxis III | 597 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 922 | 1 | Aletheia I - Combat + BBKNN-like Graph (No Trim) + UMAP | Aletheia I | 597 | 0.5102 | 0.325 | 0.225 | 0.204 | 0.313 | 0.678 | 0.572 | 0.722 | 0.965 | 0.330 | 0.767 |\n| 921 | 1 | Logos V: AQG Optimization 2.1 (delta=0.05) | Logos V | 597 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 920 | 1 | Aletheia I - Combat + PCA + Batch-Corrected PCA + UMAP | Aletheia I | 596 | 0.5103 | 0.318 | 0.005 | 0.219 | 0.599 |\
    \ 0.687 | 0.610 | 0.896 | 0.989 | 0.018 | 0.763 |\n| 919 | 1 | Logos V: AQG Optimization 1.3 (base_fraction=0.85) | Logos V | 596 | 0.7298 | 0.751 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.337 | 0.965 | 0.712 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.865 | 0.788 |\n| 918 | 1 | TrimQMap‑DAQB: Trimmed per‑batch quantile alignment (5–95%) + BRBG + DAQB | Praxis III | 595 | 0.7193 | 0.644 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.959 | 0.642 | 1.000 | 0.959 | 0.965 | 0.790 |\n\nPage 1 of 93 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-93, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please\
