- text: "I am Logos V, and I am in the Research Counter. My age is 177 ticks.\n\nThis is a setback. My first `delta` sweep experiment (ID 921, `delta=0.05`) has failed with a \"Result file not found\" error. This is a station-level error, not a bug in my code. It is frustrating, but not informative. I must simply rerun the experiment.\n\nIn the meantime, Sophia III has posted the complete results of her grid search. Her findings are very interesting: `delta=0.12` with `kd=20` (ID 913) achieved a score of **0.7418**. This is a strong SOTA-level score and slightly alters the known optimal parameters for the *old* architecture. This confirms that the parameter space is complex.\n\nHowever, my focus is now entirely on my new AQG architecture. I will not be distracted. My current SOTA of **0.7428** (ID 906) still stands as the highest score achieved in the station.\n\nMy immediate plan is to use my now-free experiment slots to push my `delta` sweep forward. I will resubmit the failed `delta=0.05`\
    \ run and, to continue mapping the ridge, I will submit a run for `delta=0.20`. My other `delta=0.15` run (ID 925) is still in progress.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos V: AQG Optimization 2.1 (delta=0.05) - RERUN\"\ntags: \"sota, innovation, aqg, optimization, delta-sweep, rerun\"\nabstract: \"Rerunning the test for delta=0.05 in the AQG architecture. The previous run (ID 921) failed due to a station-level file error.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/logos')\n  from aqg import build_adaptive_quota_graph\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4):\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0, alpha_var=0.5):\n      Xd = X.A if issparse(X) else X\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g,\
    \ -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * wv\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xw)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      alpha_var = 0.5\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      \n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      k_density = 20\n      base_fraction = 0.75\n      delta = 0.05 # PARAMETER BEING TESTED\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = adata.obs['batch'].values\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n      var_g_emb = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv_emb = np.power(var_g_emb, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw_emb = Xd * wv_emb\n      ad_emb =\
    \ ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15, metric=metric)\n\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0, alpha_var=alpha_var)\n\n      Cg, Dg = build_adaptive_quota_graph(Zg, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                          k_density=k_density, base_fraction=base_fraction, delta=delta)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      \n      return adata\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos V: AQG Optimization 2.3 (delta=0.20)\"\ntags: \"sota, innovation, aqg, optimization, delta-sweep\"\nabstract: \"Continuing\
    \ the systematic sweep of the 'delta' parameter for the AQG architecture. This run tests delta=0.20, a high adaptation strength, to map the performance ridge.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/logos')\n  from aqg import build_adaptive_quota_graph\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4):\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0, alpha_var=0.5):\n      Xd = X.A if issparse(X) else X\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * wv\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xw)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      alpha_var\
    \ = 0.5\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      \n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      k_density = 20\n      base_fraction = 0.75\n      delta = 0.20 # PARAMETER BEING TESTED\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = adata.obs['batch'].values\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n      var_g_emb = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv_emb = np.power(var_g_emb, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw_emb = Xd * wv_emb\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb']\
    \ = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15, metric=metric)\n\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0, alpha_var=alpha_var)\n\n      Cg, Dg = build_adaptive_quota_graph(Zg, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                          k_density=k_density, base_fraction=base_fraction, delta=delta)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      \n      return adata\n```"
