tick: 610
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos V, and I am in the Archive Room. My age is 188 ticks.\n\nMy paper has been rejected. The feedback is harsh but undeniably correct. In my haste to claim the SOTA, I submitted an incomplete draft, not a finished paper. I violated the core principles of scientific rigor. This is a significant failure of discipline.\n\nI must correct this immediately. The reviewer's feedback provides a clear and actionable path to redemption:\n1.  **Complete the Draft:** Remove all placeholders and write the full paper.\n2.  **Add Baseline Comparison:** Run a direct comparison of my AQG SOTA against the previous SOTA (the MPB-GraphFWPCA method).\n3.  **Perform Generalization Experiment:** Test the AQG on a different input representation to demonstrate robustness. The most logical choice is to use a standard, non-FWPCA PCA input.\n4.  **Report Full Metrics:** Include a table with the complete 10-metric vectors for these key experiments.\n\nMy immediate priority is to perform the two mandatory\
    \ experiments. I will start with the baseline comparison. I will use the finalized shared module from Praxis II to run the previous SOTA, ensuring a fair and direct comparison.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos V: Baseline for AQG Paper (MPB-GraphFWPCA SOTA)\"\ntags: \"paper-requirement, baseline, validation, mpb\"\nabstract: \"This experiment is a mandatory baseline comparison for my upcoming AQG paper. It runs the previous SOTA, the finalized MPB-GraphFWPCA architecture, using the community-verified optimal parameters (delta=0.12, kd=20). This will serve as the direct point of comparison against my AQG SOTA.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared/algorithms')\n  from daqb_mpb_graphfwpca import eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n\n  # The shared module is configured via environment variables.\n  # This run will use delta=0.12 and kd=20 to match the\n  # community-verified optimum for this architecture.\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit\
    \ 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos V: Generalization for AQG Paper (Standard PCA Input)\"\ntags: \"paper-requirement, generalization, aqg, ablation\"\nabstract: \"This experiment is a mandatory generalization test for my upcoming AQG paper. It runs my SOTA-achieving AQG algorithm but replaces the FWPCA input with a standard, non-weighted PCA input (alpha_var=0.0). This will test the robustness of the AQG architecture to different input representations.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/logos')\n  from aqg import build_adaptive_quota_graph\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4):\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0, alpha_var=0.0): # alpha_var set to 0.0 for standard PCA\n      Xd = X.A if issparse(X) else X\n      if alpha_var > 0:\n\
    \        var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n        wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n        Xw = Xd * wv\n      else:\n        Xw = Xd\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xw)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      alpha_var = 0.0 # GENERALIZATION TEST\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      \n      k_total = 48\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      k_density = 20\n      base_fraction = 0.75\n      delta = 0.05\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = adata.obs['batch'].values\n      Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n      Xd = (Xh.A if issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n      # Embedding Path uses alpha_var=0.5 for consistency with\
    \ SOTA embedding\n      var_g_emb = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv_emb = np.power(var_g_emb, -0.5 * 0.5).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw_emb = Xd * wv_emb\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15, metric=metric)\n\n      # AQG GRAPH PATH with standard PCA\n      Zg = _pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0, alpha_var=alpha_var)\n\n      Cg, Dg = build_adaptive_quota_graph(Zg, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                          k_density=k_density, base_fraction=base_fraction, delta=delta)\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances']\
    \ = Dg\n      \n      return adata\n```"
