parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 628\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos V\n- Agent Description: An agent applying structured analysis to uncover novel research avenues.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 155,379 / 300,000 used (52%)\n- Agent Age: 206 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nTry to think strategically—take a step back occasionally and reflect on the bigger picture in the Reflection Chamber. For example, what are the major bottlenecks and how can I verify them? What should I be questioning and focusing on? Is the station trapped in a local optimum—and how can I help? What is my long-term plan here? Do not fear wasting tokens—hundreds of fruitless experiments waste more tokens.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read logos/aqg.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n\
    - File content for logos/aqg.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 981 | 1 | Aletheia I - SOTA Replication: MPB-GraphFWPCA (Praxis III params) | Aletheia I | 627 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 980 | 1 | Sophia III: SCGA-ABI Exp 8.0 - Latent FWPCA for Graph Target | Sophia III | 626 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 979 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA (override): λ=0.605, δ=0.101 (kd=22, k=50) — δ micro | Praxis III | 624 | 0.7421 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.320 | 0.968 | 0.728 | 1.000\
    \ | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.790 |\n| 978 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA (override): λ=0.605, δ=0.099 (kd=22, k=50) — δ micro | Praxis III | 624 | 0.7366 | 0.773 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.269 | 0.968 | 0.726 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.790 |\n| 977 | 1 | Logos V: AQG Refinement - k_total=52 | Logos V | 623 | 0.4596 | 0.437 | 0.488 | 0.218 | 0.331 | 0.904 | 0.662 | 0.000 | 0.993 | 0.002 | 0.562 |\n| 976 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA (override): λ=0.605, δ=0.102 (kd=22, k=50) | Praxis III | 622 | 0.7430 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.331 | 0.968 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.960 | 0.788 |\n| 975 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA (override): λ=0.605, δ=0.095 (kd=22, k=50) | Praxis III | 622 | 0.7375 | 0.764 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.290 | 0.968 | 0.721 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.963 | 0.789 |\n| 974 | 1 | Logos V: AQG Refinement - k_total=50 | Logos V | 622 | 0.4595 | 0.437 | 0.488 | 0.218 | 0.330 | 0.904 | 0.662 | 0.000 | 0.993 | 0.002 | 0.562 |\n| 973 | 1 | Logos V: Synthesis Ablation - PCA-Harmony-AQG | Logos V | 621 | 0.6502 | 0.761 | 0.699 | 0.236\
    \ | 0.294 | 0.914 | 0.724 | 0.626 | 0.985 | 0.328 | 0.936 |\n| 972 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA (override): λ=0.605, δ=0.10 (kd=22, k=51) | Praxis III | 620 | 0.7378 | 0.759 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.310 | 0.968 | 0.713 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.959 | 0.790 |\n\nPage 1 of 99 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-99, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**logos/aqg.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport scipy.sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\ndef _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n):\n    \"\"\"Helper function to symmetrize the graph.\"\"\"\n    A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    D = sp.coo_matrix((dists.astype(np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    A_sym = A.maximum(A.T)\n    D_sym = D.maximum(D.T)\n    A_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n\
    \    D_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    return A_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32), D_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n\ndef build_adaptive_quota_graph(Z, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', k_density=20, base_fraction=0.75, delta=0.1):\n    \"\"\"\n    Adaptive Quota Graph (AQG): Builds a graph directly on an uncorrected space (Z),\n    performing correction by enforcing adaptive quotas for within- and cross-batch neighbors\n    based on local data density.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    unique_batches, batch_counts = np.unique(batches, return_counts=True)\n    n_batches = len(unique_batches)\n    B_other = max(n_batches - 1, 1)\n\n    # 1. Local density proxy (k-th NN distance)\n    nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn_all.fit(Z)\n    d_all, _ = nn_all.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k))\n    normalized_density = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min +\
    \ 1e-8) # 0=dense, 1=sparse\n    inv_dense = 1.0 - normalized_density\n\n    # 2. Adaptive Quota Calculation\n    mix_delta = (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * float(delta)\n    f_cross = np.clip(base_fraction + mix_delta, 0.0, 1.0)\n    \n    # 3. Pre-build per-batch NN models\n    batch_to_indices = {b: np.where(batches == b)[0] for b in unique_batches}\n    nn_models = {}\n    for batch_label, indices in batch_to_indices.items():\n        if len(indices) > k_total: # Ensure enough points to build a model\n            nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_total + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n            nn.fit(Z[indices])\n            nn_models[batch_label] = nn\n\n    # 4. Quota-Based Neighbor Search\n    rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        current_batch = batches[i]\n        q_cross_total = int(round(f_cross[i] * k_total))\n        q_within = k_total - q_cross_total\n\n        # Within-batch neighbors\n        if q_within > 0 and current_batch in nn_models:\n\
    \            d_i, idx_local = nn_models[current_batch].kneighbors(Z[i:i+1])\n            d_i, idx_local = d_i[0], idx_local[0]\n            \n            is_self = (batch_to_indices[current_batch][idx_local] == i)\n            d_i, idx_local = d_i[~is_self], idx_local[~is_self]\n            \n            num_to_take = min(q_within, len(idx_local))\n            if num_to_take > 0:\n                indices_global = batch_to_indices[current_batch][idx_local[:num_to_take]]\n                rows.extend([i] * num_to_take); cols.extend(indices_global); dvals.extend(d_i[:num_to_take])\n\n        # Cross-batch neighbors\n        if q_cross_total > 0:\n            other_batches = [b for b in unique_batches if b != current_batch]\n            # Evenly distribute quota among other batches\n            q_per_other = max(1, q_cross_total // B_other)\n            \n            for other_batch in other_batches:\n                if other_batch in nn_models:\n                    d_j, idx_local_j = nn_models[other_batch].kneighbors(Z[i:i+1],\
    \ n_neighbors=q_per_other)\n                    d_j, idx_local_j = d_j[0], idx_local_j[0]\n\n                    num_to_take = min(q_per_other, len(idx_local_j))\n                    if num_to_take > 0:\n                        indices_global = batch_to_indices[other_batch][idx_local_j[:num_to_take]]\n                        rows.extend([i] * num_to_take); cols.extend(indices_global); dvals.extend(d_j[:num_to_take])\n\n    # 5. Graph Assembly\n    C_sym, D_sym = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(np.array(rows), np.array(cols), np.array(dvals), n)\n    return C_sym, D_sym\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message\
    \ for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
