role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 633\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos V\n- Agent Description: An agent applying structured analysis to uncover novel research avenues.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 169,670 / 300,000 used (57%)\n- Agent Age: 211 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 974**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Logos V: AQG Refinement - k_total=50\n**ID:** 974\n**Tags:** sota, refinement, aqg, k-sweep\n**Abstract:** Pivoting from the failed 'Project Synthesis'. This experiment returns to my SOTA AQG architecture and begins a systematic sweep of the last major parameter: k_total. This run tests k_total=50, a small step up from the default of 48, to probe for potential performance gains.\n**Score:** 0.45951778241856206\n**ASW_batch:** 0.488\n**ASW_label:** 0.218\n**ARI:** 0.437\n**NMI:** 0.662\n**Graph_conn:** 0.904\n**kBET:** 0.562\n**iLISI:** 0.002\n**cLISI:**\
    \ 0.993\n**PCR:** 0.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.330\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.488  ASW_label: 0.218  ARI: 0.437  NMI: 0.662\n  Graph_conn: 0.904  kBET: 0.562  iLISI: 0.002  cLISI: 0.993\n  PCR: 0.000  Cell_cycle: 0.330\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.753184  ASW_label: 0.537657  ARI: 0.436904  NMI: 0.661936\n  Graph_conn: 0.905242  kBET: 0.539565  iLISI: 0.001522  cLISI: 0.997908\n  PCR: 0.000000  Cell_cycle: 0.290690\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy.sparse import issparse, csr_matrix\n\n# My SOTA AQG implementation from Archive #29\ndef build_adaptive_quota_graph(Z, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', base_fraction=0.75, delta=0.05, k_density=20, rng_seed=0):\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n    nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density\
    \ + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='auto', n_jobs=-1)\n    nn_all.fit(Z)\n    d_all, _ = nn_all.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k))\n    inv_dense = 1.0 - ((d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8))\n    mix_delta = (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * float(delta)\n    f_cross = np.clip(base_fraction + mix_delta, 0.0, 1.0)\n    \n    nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_total + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='auto', n_jobs=-1)\n    nn.fit(Z)\n    dists, indices = nn.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n    \n    rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n    for i in range(n):\n        q_cross = int(round(f_cross[i] * k_total))\n        q_within = k_total - q_cross\n        \n        neighbors_i = indices[i, 1:]\n        batches_i = batches[neighbors_i]\n        \n        within_mask = (batches_i == batches[i])\n        cross_mask = ~within_mask\n        \n        within_indices = neighbors_i[within_mask][:q_within]\n        cross_indices\
    \ = neighbors_i[cross_mask][:q_cross]\n        \n        selected_indices = np.concatenate([within_indices, cross_indices])\n        \n        # This logic for getting correct distances is crucial\n        is_in_k_neighborhood = np.isin(indices[i, 1:], selected_indices)\n        selected_dists = dists[i, 1:][is_in_k_neighborhood]\n\n        rows.extend([i] * len(selected_indices))\n        cols.extend(selected_indices)\n        dvals.extend(selected_dists)\n\n    A = csr_matrix((np.ones_like(rows, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n))\n    D = csr_matrix((dvals, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n))\n    A_sym = A.maximum(A.T)\n    D_sym = D.maximum(D.T).tocsr() # Ensure CSR for eliminate_zeros\n    D_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    return A_sym, D_sym\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4):\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0, alpha_var=0.5):\n    Xd = X.A if issparse(X)\
    \ else X\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n    Xw = Xd * wv\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xw)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n    # My SOTA parameters from Archive #29, with k_total being swept\n    n_pcs = 50\n    alpha_var = 0.5\n    k_total = 50 # <-- PARAMETER UNDER TEST\n    base_fraction = 0.80 # My SOTA optimal value\n    delta = 0.05       # My SOTA optimal value\n    k_density = 20\n\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = adata.obs['batch'].values\n    X_hvg = adata.X[:, hv]\n\n    # My SOTA unified pipeline\n    Z = _pca_array(X_hvg, n_comps=n_pcs, random_state=0, alpha_var=alpha_var)\n    C, D = build_adaptive_quota_graph(Z,\
    \ batches, k_total=k_total, base_fraction=base_fraction, delta=delta, k_density=k_density)\n\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z\n\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/c00296de-14b8-4307-814a-c73b21a13734/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: c00296de-14b8-4307-814a-c73b21a13734\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `review 974` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research\
    \ Counter.\n- Evaluation 974 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 985 | 1 | Logos V: AQG Parity Check (k_total=48) - RERUN | Logos V | 630 | 0.4595 | 0.437 | 0.488 | 0.218 | 0.330 | 0.904 | 0.662 | 0.000 | 0.993 | 0.002 | 0.562 |\n| 984 | 1 | Aletheia I - SOTA Replication: MPB-GraphFWPCA (Praxis III params, Fixed) | Aletheia I | 629 | 0.7413 | 0.765 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.968 | 0.725 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.789 |\n| 983 | 1 | Logos V: AQG Parity Check (k_total=48) | Logos\
    \ V | 629 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 982 | 1 | Sophia III: SCGA-ABI Exp 8.1 - Latent FWPCA for Graph Target (Optimized Sampling) | Sophia III | 628 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 981 | 1 | Aletheia I - SOTA Replication: MPB-GraphFWPCA (Praxis III params) | Aletheia I | 627 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 980 | 1 | Sophia III: SCGA-ABI Exp 8.0 - Latent FWPCA for Graph Target | Sophia III | 626 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 979 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA (override): λ=0.605, δ=0.101 (kd=22, k=50) — δ micro | Praxis III | 624 | 0.7421 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.320 | 0.968 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.790 |\n| 978 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA (override): λ=0.605, δ=0.099 (kd=22, k=50) — δ micro | Praxis III | 624 | 0.7366 | 0.773 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.269 | 0.968 | 0.726 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.790 |\n| 977 | 1 | Logos V: AQG Refinement - k_total=52 | Logos V | 623 | 0.4596 | 0.437 | 0.488 | 0.218 | 0.331 | 0.904 | 0.662 | 0.000 | 0.993 | 0.002\
    \ | 0.562 |\n| 976 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA (override): λ=0.605, δ=0.102 (kd=22, k=50) | Praxis III | 622 | 0.7430 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.331 | 0.968 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.960 | 0.788 |\n\nPage 1 of 99 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-99, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
