    \ 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.596816  NMI: 0.708633\n  Graph_conn: 0.908597  kBET: 0.753408  iLISI: 0.023368  cLISI: 0.997509\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.287468\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 987\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed undefined variable error in submission v2. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission (v1) used the variable `Xd` on line 44 without defining it in the function scope:\n\n```python\nvar_g_emb = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n```\n\nThe variable `Xd` was only created locally inside the `_pca_array` helper function and was not available in the `eliminate_batch_effect_fn` function where it was referenced. This caused a `NameError: name 'Xd' is not defined`.\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded a single line before the problematic code to properly define `Xd` by converting `X_hvg` (which was already available) to a dense array if sparse:\n\n```python\n# FIX: Define Xd before using it\nXd = X_hvg.A if issparse(X_hvg)\
    \ else X_hvg\nvar_g_emb = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n```\n\nThis follows the same pattern used in the `_pca_array` function (line 15 of the original code) to convert sparse matrices to dense numpy arrays.\n\n## Verification\n- Created submission_v2.py with the fix\n- Monitored evaluation for 300 seconds\n- Code executed without crashing\n- Exit code 0 (success - code is running)\n\n## Technical Details\nThe fix ensures that `Xd` is properly defined as a dense numpy array before attempting to call the `.var()` method on it. This is necessary because the subsequent code performs variance calculations and weighted transformations that require a dense array representation.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy.sparse import issparse\n\
    \n# IMPORTING FROM THE CORRECT, VALIDATED MASTER SCRIPT\nsys.path.append('storage/logos')\nfrom aqg_sota_v1 import build_adaptive_quota_graph\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4):\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0, alpha_var=0.5):\n    Xd = X.A if issparse(X) else X\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n    Xw = Xd * wv\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xw)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n    # Original SOTA parameters from ID 928\n    n_pcs = 50\n    alpha_var = 0.5\n    k_total = 48\n    base_fraction = 0.80\n    delta = 0.05\n    k_density = 20\n\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000,\
    \ inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = adata.obs['batch'].values\n    X_hvg = adata.X[:, hv]\n\n    # My SOTA unified pipeline, using the master script\n    Z = _pca_array(X_hvg, n_comps=n_pcs, random_state=0, alpha_var=alpha_var)\n    C, D = build_adaptive_quota_graph(Z, batches, k_total=k_total, base_fraction=base_fraction, delta=delta, k_density=k_density)\n\n    # Re-adding the dual-path embedding from the original SOTA paper for full parity\n    # FIX: Define Xd before using it\n    Xd = X_hvg.A if issparse(X_hvg) else X_hvg\n    var_g_emb = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    wv_emb = np.power(var_g_emb, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n    Xw_emb = Xd * wv_emb\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=60, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    Z_emb = ad_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(Z_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n\
    \    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/c4b0a5ca-658d-4c56-b51c-88b92527d5c2/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: c4b0a5ca-658d-4c56-b51c-88b92527d5c2\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nIt is highly recommended to preview all papers in the Archive Room (`/execute_action{goto archive}` and `/execute_action{preview all}`) if you have not done so already. Previewing papers consumes only a small amount of tokens but can save you many ticks by avoiding\
