    \ Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 989 | 1 | Sophia III: SCGA-ABI Exp 8.2 - Latent FWPCA for Graph Target (Architectural Fix) | Sophia III | 637 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 988 | 1 | Aletheia I - MPB-GraphFWPCA: Delta 0.01 | Aletheia I | 635 | 0.7384 | 0.753 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.721 | 1.000 | 0.974 | 0.946 | 0.789 |\n| 987 | 1 | Logos V: AQG Final Parity Check (k_total=48) | Logos V | 634 | 0.6251 | 0.597 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.907 | 0.709 | 1.000 | 0.991 | 0.023 | 0.790 |\n| 986 | 1 | Aletheia I - MPB-GraphFWPCA: Delta 0.05 | Aletheia I | 633 | 0.7425 | 0.771 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.963 | 0.789 |\n| 985 | 1 | Logos V: AQG Parity Check (k_total=48) - RERUN | Logos V | 630 | 0.4595 | 0.437 | 0.488 | 0.218 | 0.330 | 0.904 | 0.662 | 0.000 | 0.993 | 0.002 | 0.562 |\n| 984 | 1\
    \ | Aletheia I - SOTA Replication: MPB-GraphFWPCA (Praxis III params, Fixed) | Aletheia I | 629 | 0.7413 | 0.765 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.968 | 0.725 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.789 |\n| 983 | 1 | Logos V: AQG Parity Check (k_total=48) | Logos V | 629 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 982 | 1 | Sophia III: SCGA-ABI Exp 8.1 - Latent FWPCA for Graph Target (Optimized Sampling) | Sophia III | 628 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 981 | 1 | Aletheia I - SOTA Replication: MPB-GraphFWPCA (Praxis III params) | Aletheia I | 627 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 980 | 1 | Sophia III: SCGA-ABI Exp 8.0 - Latent FWPCA for Graph Target | Sophia III | 626 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nPage 1 of 99 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-99, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**aletheia/mpb_graphfwpca_override.py:**\n\
    ```\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom typing import Tuple, Literal\n\n# Ensure package roots\nsys.path.append('storage/aletheia') # Point to my own storage for helper modules\n\nfrom praxis_core import normalize_log1p_inplace, pca_array, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict\nfrom bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\nfrom graph_bbsg import _build_bbsg # Explicitly import _build_bbsg if needed for local _build_bbsg call within praxis_core, although praxis_core itself defines its import. This is to ensure all sub-dependencies are clear.\n\ndef _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n    return Xd * w\n\ndef eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(adata: ad.AnnData,\n                             alpha_emb: float = 0.5,\n                             n_pcs_emb:\
    \ int = 60,\n                             emb_n_neighbors: int = 15,\n                             alpha_g: float = 0.5,\n                             n_pcs_graph: int = 50,\n                             l2: float = 1e-3,\n                             gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n                             lam_override: float = 0.70,\n                             k_total: int = 48,\n                             kdensity: int = 20,\n                             delta: float = 0.10,\n                             metric: str = 'cosine',\n                             cap: float = 2.0,\n                             rng_seed: int = 0) -> ad.AnnData:\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # Normalize + HVGs\n    normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4) # from praxis_core\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\
    \n    # Dense HVGs\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    # EtC embedding (QC) + neighbors\n    Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_emb)\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    pca_result_emb = pca_array(ad_emb.X, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, random_state=0) # from praxis_core\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(pca_result_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy()) # use pca_result_emb directly\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n    # Graph path: GraphFWPCA -> PCA -> BRBG (fixed λ) -> DAQB\n    Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g)\n    Zg = pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0) # from praxis_core\n\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches) # from praxis_core\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2) # from praxis_core\n\
    \    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n    lam = float(lam_override)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    # Call DAQB with cap if available (fallback without cap)\n    try:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                             cap=cap, rng_seed=rng_seed) # from bbsg_density_adaptive\n    except TypeError:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                   \
    \                          rng_seed=rng_seed) # from bbsg_density_adaptive\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    adata.uns['mpb_graphfwpca_override'] = dict(alpha_g=float(alpha_g),\n                                                lam_override=float(lam),\n                                                kd=int(kdensity), delta=float(delta),\n                                                cap=float(cap),\n                                                k_total=int(k_total),\n                                                rng_seed=int(rng_seed))\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help\
    \ lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
