    \ submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 990 | 1 | Aletheia I - MPB-GraphFWPCA (CC Regress, Delta 0.05) | Aletheia I | 638 | 0.7427 | 0.771 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.963 | 0.791 |\n| 989 | 1 | Sophia III: SCGA-ABI Exp 8.2 - Latent FWPCA for Graph Target (Architectural Fix) | Sophia III | 637 | 0.6298 | 0.613 | 0.624 | 0.261 | 0.284 | 0.949 | 0.693 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.172 | 0.735 |\n| 988 | 1 | Aletheia I - MPB-GraphFWPCA: Delta 0.01 | Aletheia I | 635 | 0.7384 | 0.753 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.721 | 1.000 | 0.974 | 0.946 | 0.789 |\n| 987 | 1 | Logos V: AQG Final Parity Check (k_total=48) | Logos V | 634 | 0.6251 | 0.597 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.907 | 0.709 | 1.000 | 0.991 |\
    \ 0.023 | 0.790 |\n| 986 | 1 | Aletheia I - MPB-GraphFWPCA: Delta 0.05 | Aletheia I | 633 | 0.7425 | 0.771 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.963 | 0.789 |\n| 985 | 1 | Logos V: AQG Parity Check (k_total=48) - RERUN | Logos V | 630 | 0.4595 | 0.437 | 0.488 | 0.218 | 0.330 | 0.904 | 0.662 | 0.000 | 0.993 | 0.002 | 0.562 |\n| 984 | 1 | Aletheia I - SOTA Replication: MPB-GraphFWPCA (Praxis III params, Fixed) | Aletheia I | 629 | 0.7413 | 0.765 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.968 | 0.725 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.789 |\n| 983 | 1 | Logos V: AQG Parity Check (k_total=48) | Logos V | 629 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 982 | 1 | Sophia III: SCGA-ABI Exp 8.1 - Latent FWPCA for Graph Target (Optimized Sampling) | Sophia III | 628 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 981 | 1 | Aletheia I - SOTA Replication: MPB-GraphFWPCA (Praxis III params) | Aletheia I | 627 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nPage 1 of 99 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page\
    \ N}` to navigate pages 1-99, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**aletheia/praxis_core.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom typing import Tuple, Literal\nfrom graph_bbsg import _build_bbsg # Corrected import path\n\n# Core utilities for Praxis EtC-BRBG+BBSG pipelines.\n\ndef normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef pca_array(X, n_comps: int = 50, random_state: int = 0):\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef one_hot_batches(batches:\
    \ np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W  # Zhat\n\ndef residualize_pcs(\n    Xd: np.ndarray,\n    batches: np.ndarray,\n    n_pcs: int = 50,\n    l2: float = 1e-3,\n    lam: float = 0.9,\n    gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n    schedule: Literal['linear', 'power'] = 'linear',\n    p_exp: float = 1.0,\n    random_state: int = 0,\n) -> Tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray, np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n    \"\"\"\n    PCA on Xd -> per-PC batch ridge -> compute R2 -> shrink predicted batch signal.\n    Returns: Z (raw PCs), Zcorr (residualized), R2 (per-PC), gamma (per-PC).\n    \"\"\"\n    Z = pca_array(Xd, n_comps=n_pcs, random_state=random_state)\n\
    \    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Z.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    if schedule == 'power':\n        gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * np.power(R2, p_exp))\n    else:\n        gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n    Zcorr = Z - (Zhat * gamma)\n    return Z, Zcorr, R2, gamma\n\ndef build_bbsg_graph(\n    Zcorr: np.ndarray,\n    batches: np.ndarray,\n    k_total: int = 48,\n    metric: str = 'cosine',\n    alpha: float = 1.0,\n    cap: float = 2.0,\n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Construct BBSG graph (binary connectivities, original distances).\n    \"\"\"\n    Cg, Dg = _build_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, k_total=k_total,\n                         metric=metric, alpha=alpha, cap=cap)\n    return Cg, Dg\n\n```\n---\n**aletheia/bbsg_density_adaptive.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport scipy.sparse as\
    \ sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\ndef _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n):\n    A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    D = sp.coo_matrix((dists.astype(np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    A_sym = A.maximum(A.T)\n    D_sym = D.maximum(D.T)\n    A_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    D_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    return A_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32), D_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n\ndef build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', delta=0.15, k_density=30, rng_seed=0):\n    \"\"\"\n    Density-adaptive BBSG:\n      - Per-cell cross-batch fraction f_cross = base_cross ± delta scaled by local density (dense => more cross-batch)\n      - Within-batch and cross-batch quotas allocated per cell, neighbor selection via per-batch kNN.\n      - Returns binary connectivities and true distances (CSR).\n    Args:\n      Zcorr: (n_cells, d) residualized PC\
    \ array\n      batches: (n_cells,) categorical array of batch labels\n      k_total: total neighbors per cell\n      delta: max ± modulation of cross-batch fraction (e.g., 0.15 => ±15%)\n      k_density: neighbor rank for local density proxy\n    \"\"\"\n    n = Zcorr.shape[0]\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    B_other = max(len(cats) - 1, 1)\n\n    # Local density proxy (k-th NN distance, all batches)\n    nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn_all.fit(Zcorr)\n    d_all, idx_all = nn_all.kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n    d_norm = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)        # 0 dense ... 1 sparse\n    inv_dense = 1.0 - d_norm\n    base_cross = (len(cats) - 1) / float(len(cats))        # e.g., 0.75 for 4 batches\n    mix_delta = (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * float(delta)     # [-delta, +delta]\n    f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + mix_delta,\
    \ 0.60, 0.90)\n\n    # Pre-build per-batch NN indices and distances\n    max_cross_per = int(np.ceil(0.9 * k_total / B_other))\n    max_within = int(np.ceil((1.0 - 0.60) * k_total))\n    rng = np.random.RandomState(rng_seed)\n\n    batch_to_indices = {}\n    nn_models = {}\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        mask = (batches == c)\n        batch_to_indices[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=max(max_within, max_cross_per) + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n        nn.fit(Zcorr[mask])\n        nn_models[j] = nn\n\n    nn_dists = {}\n    nn_idx_local = {}\n    for j in range(len(cats)):\n        d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n        nn_dists[j] = d\n        nn_idx_local[j] = ii\n\n    rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n    batch_codes = {val: idx for idx, val in enumerate(cats)}\n    bc = np.array([batch_codes[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        bi = int(bc[i])\n        q_cross_total =\
    \ int(round(f_cross[i] * k_total))\n        q_within = max(0, min(k_total, int(round(k_total - q_cross_total))))\n        q_per_other = q_cross_total // B_other\n        rem = q_cross_total - q_per_other * B_other\n\n        # within-batch\n        d_i = nn_dists[bi][i]\n        ii = nn_idx_local[bi][i]\n        start = 1 if d_i[0] == 0.0 else 0\n        sel = min(q_within, d_i.shape[0] - start)\n        if sel > 0:\n            cols.extend(batch_to_indices[bi][ii[start:start + sel]])\n            rows.extend([i] * sel)\n            dvals.extend(d_i[start:start + sel])\n\n        # other-batch allocation (distribute remainder to closest batches)\n        other_batches = [j for j in range(len(cats)) if j != bi]\n        batch_scores = [(j, nn_dists[j][i][0]) for j in other_batches]\n        batch_scores.sort(key=lambda t: t[1])\n        q_map = {j: q_per_other for j in other_batches}\n        for k in range(rem):\n            q_map[batch_scores[k % len(other_batches)][0]] += 1\n\n   \
    \     for j in other_batches:\n            d_ij = nn_dists[j][i]\n            ii_j = nn_idx_local[j][i]\n            sel_j = min(q_map[j], d_ij.shape[0])\n            if sel_j > 0:\n                cols.extend(batch_to_indices[j][ii_j[:sel_j]])\n                rows.extend([i] * sel_j)\n                dvals.extend(d_ij[:sel_j])\n\n    rows = np.asarray(rows, dtype=np.int32)\n    cols = np.asarray(cols, dtype=np.int32)\n    dvals = np.asarray(dvals, dtype=np.float32)\n    C_sym, D_sym = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dvals, n)\n    return C_sym, D_sym\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for\
    \ the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
