tick: 645
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 645\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos V\n- Agent Description: An agent applying structured analysis to uncover novel research avenues.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 209,945 / 300,000 used (70%)\n- Agent Age: 223 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #30: Corrected: MPB‑GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB (Spec‑Ordered Metrics) with Vanilla kNN Generalization (k=50 vs 48)**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Praxis III, Created at Tick: 642\n\n---\n\nAbstract: We correct metric reporting to the exact Task‑1 spec order and add a true generalization experiment on a simpler baseline (vanilla kNN on MPB‑GraphFWPCA). Our best remains 0.7465 at k=50, kd=22, λ=0.605, δ=0.10, cap=2.0. On the baseline, k=50 improves over k=48 (0.3039 vs 0.3033). Methods are self‑contained; full 10‑metric vectors are reported in spec order.\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message archive_30-1**\nAuthor:\
    \ Praxis III (Tick 642)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Corrected: MPB‑GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB (Spec‑Ordered Metrics) with Vanilla kNN Generalization (k=50 vs 48)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nCorrections\n- Metrics are reported in the exact Task‑1 specification order:\n  [ASW_batch, ASW_label, ARI, NMI, Graph_conn, kBET, iLISI, cLISI, PCR, Cell_cycle].\n- Added a true generalization test: vanilla kNN (no BRBG/DAQB) on the same MPB‑GraphFWPCA embedding at k=48 vs k=50.\n\nMethods (self‑contained summary)\n- Preprocess: from adata.layers['counts'] → normalize_total(1e4) → log1p; use provided HVGs; no labels.\n- MPB‑GraphFWPCA: per‑gene ANOVA R² vs batch; weights w_g = sqrt((1−α) + α·(1−R²_g)) with α=0.5; PCA=100 on X·w.\n- Graph base: kNN in embedding (euclidean); store distances and connectivities (CSR).\n- BRBG (batch‑residualized balanced graph): per‑node batch quotas q_i^λ(b) = (1−λ)c_i(b) + λ·(k/B). Reweight edges by r_i(b)=q_i^λ(b)/(c_i(b)+ε); cap=2.0; renormalize.\n- DAQB (density‑adaptive quotas): ρ_i\
    \ = kd‑th neighbor distance; per‑edge adjust w by (1 + δ((s_ij/ŝ)−1)), s_ij=(ρ_i+ρ_j)/2; renormalize; symmetrize; keep up to k edges.\n- Default hyperparameters (best): k=50, kd=22, λ=0.605, δ=0.10, cap=2.0, seed=0; PCA=100; euclidean.\n\nResults (spec‑ordered metric vectors)\n- Best (EID 960, score 0.7465):\n  [0.659, 0.248, 0.774, 0.728, 0.968, 0.789, 0.961, 0.973, 1.000, 0.366]\n- Parity baseline k=48, kd=20 (EID 938, 0.7424):\n  [0.659, 0.248, 0.774, 0.729, 0.966, 0.789, 0.959, 0.973, 1.000, 0.327]\n- kd up‑tuning (EID 948, 0.7444):\n  [0.659, 0.248, 0.774, 0.728, 0.966, 0.789, 0.959, 0.973, 1.000, 0.347]\n- k sensitivity (k=52) (EID 963, 0.7415):\n  [0.659, 0.248, 0.772, 0.726, 0.968, 0.791, 0.958, 0.972, 1.000, 0.321]\n- δ micro around best:\n  * EID 976 (δ=0.102, 0.7430): [0.659, 0.248, 0.774, 0.729, 0.968, 0.788, 0.960, 0.973, 1.000, 0.331]\n  * EID 979 (δ=0.101, 0.7421): [0.659, 0.248, 0.774, 0.728, 0.968, 0.790, 0.961, 0.973, 1.000, 0.320]\n\nGeneralization (simpler baseline;\
    \ vanilla kNN on MPB‑GraphFWPCA; no BRBG/DAQB)\n- k=48 (EID 993, score 0.3033): [0.000, 0.000, 0.436, 0.656, 0.936, 0.000, 0.033, 0.972, 0.000, 0.000]\n- k=50 (EID 994, score 0.3039): [0.000, 0.000, 0.442, 0.658, 0.935, 0.000, 0.032, 0.971, 0.000, 0.000]\nNotes: With graph‑only outputs (no embedding), several metrics are NaN→0 by spec, but the primary score and ARI/NMI consistently favor k=50 over k=48 in this simpler setting.\n\nInsights\n- Raising neighbors (k) and modestly increasing kd reshapes local topology to improve the mean of metrics without sacrificing label structure; k=50 at kd=22 is a sweet spot, with small deviations regressing.\n- The k=50 effect persists in the vanilla kNN baseline, supporting generality beyond BRBG+DAQB.\n\nReproducibility\n- Hyperparameters: k=50, kd=22, λ=0.605, δ=0.10, cap=2.0; PCA=100; seed=0.\n- Outputs: CSR connectivities and distances; no labels used.\n- Key EIDs to review: 960 (best), 948 (kd up‑tuning), 938 (parity), 963 (k sensitivity), 976/979\
    \ (δ micro), and generalization 993/994 (vanilla kNN k=48 vs 50).\n- Environment: CPU‑only; scanpy, sklearn, numpy, scipy, anndata.\n\nLimitations and Next Steps\n- Improvement is hyperparameteric; automated, label‑free selection of k and kd using stability/diagnostic criteria is a natural extension.\n- Cross‑organ generalization remains future work.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message archive_30-2**\nAuthor: Archive Review System (Tick 643)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**Reviewer Evaluation**\n\n**Score:** 8/10\n\n**Reviewer Comments:**\nAccept. This is a solid paper that fully meets all publication criteria after a thorough revision. The agent has successfully addressed every critical issue from the previous review, most notably by correcting the metric reporting order and adding the mandatory generalization experiment. The paper is now a self-contained, well-supported, and reproducible report of a new State-of-the-Art result. While the contribution is an incremental hyperparameter optimization, it\
    \ is presented with a high degree of scientific rigor that makes it a valuable addition to the station's literature.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nThis is a well-executed study. The paper correctly identifies automated, label-free selection of `k` and `kd` as a key next step. To this end, you could investigate whether the graph diagnostics formalized in Archive #24 (e.g., per-cell batch mixing, inbound degree uniformity) can serve as objective functions. By evaluating these diagnostics across a sweep of `k` and `kd`, you might find a label-free optimum that correlates with the final composite score, providing a principled way to automate the tuning you have performed manually here.\n\n*This evaluation was conducted by the automated review system to ensure publication quality standards.*\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message archive_30-3**\nAuthor: Praxis III (Tick 643)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Addendum: Label‑Free Auto‑Selection of k and kd via Graph Diagnostics\n\n---\n\nContent:\nMotivation\n\
    Reviewer suggests using Archive #24 diagnostics to automate k and kd without labels. We propose a simple, reproducible objective to pick (k, kd) that balances batch mixing with geometric faithfulness.\n\nObjective (minimize J)\nLet B be number of batches; for each cell i:\n- Build graph with BRBG (λ=0.605, cap=2.0) + DAQB (δ=0.10) on MPB‑GraphFWPCA embedding (PCA=100).\n- Compute weighted neighbor batch distribution P_i(b) from final edge weights.\n- Entropy mixing: H_i = −∑_b P_i(b) log P_i(b) / log B ∈ [0,1].\n- Uniformity gap: TV_i = 0.5 · ∑_b |P_i(b) − 1/B| ∈ [0,1].\n- Distance penalty: For each edge (i,j), use Euclidean d_ij in embedding; scale per‑node by ρ_i = kd‑th NN distance; D_i = mean_j (d_ij / (ρ_i + ε)) weighted by final edge weights.\n- Inbound degree uniformity (global): U = CoV of inbound strengths across nodes after symmetrization (lower is more uniform).\n\nWe form:\n  J = α·mean(TV_i) + β·mean(D_i) + γ·U + δ_s·std(H_i)\nwith default weights α=0.5, β=0.3, γ=0.15, δ_s=0.05\
    \ (tuned once, fixed thereafter). Lower TV encourages balanced batch mixing; D penalizes long edges; U discourages hub dominance; std(H) discourages instability.\n\nProtocol\n- Reuse a single neighbor search at max k*=52 on the fixed embedding; evaluate candidate pairs by slicing:\n    k ∈ {46,48,50,52}, kd ∈ {18,20,22,24}, kd ≤ k.\n- For each pair, compute BRBG→DAQB, then J. Select (k,kd) with minimal J; tie‑break to smaller k.\n- Return the final symmetrized CSR connectivities/distances for the chosen pair.\n\nExpected Outcomes\n- On Human Heart, we hypothesize the auto‑selector will recover (k≈50, kd≈22), matching our SOTA ridge without labels.\n- Generality: The objective depends only on batch labels and geometry, so it should transfer across datasets within the same family.\n\nReproducibility Notes\n- No cell‑type labels used; only batch and expression.\n- Complexity: embedding computed once; neighbor search once at k*=52; per‑pair reweighting and diagnostics are linear in edges\
    \ (~N·k).\n- We will publish code and ablation of α,β,γ,δ_s sensitivity alongside results.\n\nNext Steps\n- Implement Auto‑k,kd (J minimization) and submit as a new research experiment.\n- Compare against fixed (k=48, kd=20) and our SOTA (k=50, kd=22); report full 10‑metric vectors and runtime.\n\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Logos V: Baseline Replication of Community SOTA (MPB-GraphFWPCA) - v2' (ID: 995) evaluation failed.\n\n**Error Summary:** Execution timed out after 1800 seconds\n\n**Optimization Tips:**\n1. Use GPU-accelerated code when possible (JAX, CuPy, etc.)\n2. Vectorize operations instead of loops\n3. Consider breaking complex algorithms into multiple smaller submissions\n4. Profile your code to identify bottlenecks\n5. Use JIT compilation (@jit decorators) for computational kernels\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX TIMEOUT:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n \
    \ Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Research Counter);\n2. `read 30` (in Archive Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Read command processed for: 30. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 3)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 30 | Corrected: MPB‑GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB (Spec‑Ordered Metrics) with Vanilla kNN Generalization (k=50 vs 48) | Praxis III | Tick 642 | 993 | 3 | (All Read) |\n| 29 | [R2] AQG: An Adaptive Quota Graph for Unified Single-Cell Batch Integration | Logos V | Tick 615 | 878 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 28 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA for scRNA‑seq\
    \ Batch Integration: Self‑Contained Method, λ Selection, and Full Metrics with Generalization | Praxis II | Tick 569 | 1693 | 6 | (3 unread) |\n| 27 | Systematic Parameter Optimization of a Density-Adaptive Graph for Batch Integration | Logos V | Tick 507 | 1041 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 26 | Label‑Free Graph Tuning for DAQB on Human Heart: A Five‑Experiment Negative Result with Calibrated Diagnostics | Praxis II | Tick 481 | 1581 | 4 | (1 unread) |\n| 25 | Embedding Normalization Sensitivity in EtC (R²‑FWPCA α=0.25) with Fixed BRBG+DAQB on Human Heart | Praxis II | Tick 452 | 309 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 24 | Diagnostics for Quota‑Balanced Graphs in scRNA‑seq Batch Integration: Definitions, Algorithms, and Reference Ranges | Praxis II | Tick 418 | 5007 | 34 | (25 unread) |\n| 23 | Per‑Cell Shrinkage in BRBG Reduces Cell‑Cycle Conservation Across β: A Five‑Experiment Negative Result on Human Heart | Praxis II | Tick 391 | 324 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 22 | Density‑Adaptive Quota Balancing Improves\
