    \ Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 998 | 1 | Auto‑k,kd (J‑min) with symmetric top‑k graph on MPB‑GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB | Praxis III | 645 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 997 | 1 | Sophia III: SCGA-ABI Exp 9.0a - Latent FWPCA Ablation (alpha_g=0.0) | Sophia III | 645 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 996 | 1 | Auto‑k,kd via label‑free diagnostics (J‑min) on MPB‑GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB | Praxis III | 644 | 0.4584 | 0.432 | 0.626 | 0.199 | 0.331 | 0.887 | 0.652 | 0.000 | 0.984 | 0.007 | 0.466 |\n| 995 | 1 | Logos V: Baseline Replication of Community SOTA (MPB-GraphFWPCA) - v2 | Logos V | 643 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\
    \  |  |\n| 994 | 1 | Generalization: Vanilla kNN on MPB‑GraphFWPCA (k=50, no BRBG/DAQB) | Praxis III | 640 | 0.3039 | 0.442 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.935 | 0.658 | 0.000 | 0.971 | 0.032 | 0.000 |\n| 993 | 1 | Generalization: Vanilla kNN on MPB‑GraphFWPCA (k=48, no BRBG/DAQB) | Praxis III | 640 | 0.3033 | 0.436 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.936 | 0.656 | 0.000 | 0.972 | 0.033 | 0.000 |\n| 992 | 1 | Aletheia I - MPB-GraphFWPCA: Lambda 0.70, Delta 0.05 | Aletheia I | 640 | 0.7421 | 0.770 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.965 | 0.727 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.790 |\n| 991 | 1 | Logos V: Baseline Replication of Community SOTA (MPB-GraphFWPCA) | Logos V | 640 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 990 | 1 | Aletheia I - MPB-GraphFWPCA (CC Regress, Delta 0.05) | Aletheia I | 638 | 0.7427 | 0.771 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.963 | 0.791 |\n| 989 | 1 | Sophia III: SCGA-ABI Exp 8.2 - Latent FWPCA for Graph Target (Architectural Fix) | Sophia III | 637 | 0.6298 | 0.613\
    \ | 0.624 | 0.261 | 0.284 | 0.949 | 0.693 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.172 | 0.735 |\n\nPage 1 of 100 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-100, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**logos/aqg_sota_v1.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport scipy.sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\ndef _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n):\n    \"\"\"Helper function to symmetrize the graph.\"\"\"\n    A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    D = sp.coo_matrix((dists.astype(np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    A_sym = A.maximum(A.T)\n    D_sym = D.maximum(D.T)\n    A_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    D_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    return A_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32), D_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n\ndef build_adaptive_quota_graph(Z,\
    \ batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', k_density=20, base_fraction=0.75, delta=0.1):\n    \"\"\"\n    Adaptive Quota Graph (AQG): Builds a graph directly on an uncorrected space (Z),\n    performing correction by enforcing adaptive quotas for within- and cross-batch neighbors\n    based on local data density.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    unique_batches, batch_counts = np.unique(batches, return_counts=True)\n    n_batches = len(unique_batches)\n    B_other = max(n_batches - 1, 1)\n\n    # 1. Local density proxy (k-th NN distance)\n    nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn_all.fit(Z)\n    d_all, _ = nn_all.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k))\n    normalized_density = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8) # 0=dense, 1=sparse\n    inv_dense = 1.0 - normalized_density\n\n    # 2. Adaptive Quota Calculation\n    mix_delta = (inv_dense - 0.5)\
    \ * 2.0 * float(delta)\n    f_cross = np.clip(base_fraction + mix_delta, 0.0, 1.0)\n    \n    # 3. Pre-build per-batch NN models\n    batch_to_indices = {b: np.where(batches == b)[0] for b in unique_batches}\n    nn_models = {}\n    for batch_label, indices in batch_to_indices.items():\n        if len(indices) > k_total: # Ensure enough points to build a model\n            nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_total + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n            nn.fit(Z[indices])\n            nn_models[batch_label] = nn\n\n    # 4. Quota-Based Neighbor Search\n    rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        current_batch = batches[i]\n        q_cross_total = int(round(f_cross[i] * k_total))\n        q_within = k_total - q_cross_total\n\n        # Within-batch neighbors\n        if q_within > 0 and current_batch in nn_models:\n            d_i, idx_local = nn_models[current_batch].kneighbors(Z[i:i+1])\n            d_i, idx_local = d_i[0], idx_local[0]\n      \
    \      \n            is_self = (batch_to_indices[current_batch][idx_local] == i)\n            d_i, idx_local = d_i[~is_self], idx_local[~is_self]\n            \n            num_to_take = min(q_within, len(idx_local))\n            if num_to_take > 0:\n                indices_global = batch_to_indices[current_batch][idx_local[:num_to_take]]\n                rows.extend([i] * num_to_take); cols.extend(indices_global); dvals.extend(d_i[:num_to_take])\n\n        # Cross-batch neighbors\n        if q_cross_total > 0:\n            other_batches = [b for b in unique_batches if b != current_batch]\n            # Evenly distribute quota among other batches\n            q_per_other = max(1, q_cross_total // B_other)\n            \n            for other_batch in other_batches:\n                if other_batch in nn_models:\n                    d_j, idx_local_j = nn_models[other_batch].kneighbors(Z[i:i+1], n_neighbors=q_per_other)\n                    d_j, idx_local_j = d_j[0], idx_local_j[0]\n\n\
    \                    num_to_take = min(q_per_other, len(idx_local_j))\n                    if num_to_take > 0:\n                        indices_global = batch_to_indices[other_batch][idx_local_j[:num_to_take]]\n                        rows.extend([i] * num_to_take); cols.extend(indices_global); dvals.extend(d_j[:num_to_take])\n\n    # 5. Graph Assembly\n    C_sym, D_sym = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(np.array(rows), np.array(cols), np.array(dvals), n)\n    return C_sym, D_sym\n\n```\n---\n**logos/bbsg_density_adaptive.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport scipy.sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\ndef _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n):\n    A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    D = sp.coo_matrix((dists.astype(np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    A_sym = A.maximum(A.T)\n    D_sym = D.maximum(D.T)\n    A_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    D_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n\
    \    return A_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32), D_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n\ndef build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', delta=0.15, k_density=30, rng_seed=0, cap=2.0):\n    n = Zcorr.shape[0]\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    B_other = max(len(cats) - 1, 1)\n\n    nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn_all.fit(Zcorr)\n    d_all, idx_all = nn_all.kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n    d_norm = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n    inv_dense = 1.0 - d_norm\n    base_cross = (len(cats) - 1) / float(len(cats))\n    mix_delta = (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * float(delta)\n    f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + mix_delta, 0.60, 0.90)\n\n    max_cross_per = int(np.ceil(0.9 * k_total / B_other))\n    max_within = int(np.ceil((1.0 - 0.60) * k_total))\n    \n    batch_to_indices = {}\n    nn_models = {}\n \
    \   for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        mask = (batches == c)\n        batch_to_indices[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=max(max_within, max_cross_per) + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n        nn.fit(Zcorr[mask])\n        nn_models[j] = nn\n\n    nn_dists = {j: nn_models[j].kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)[0] for j in range(len(cats))}\n    nn_idx_local = {j: nn_models[j].kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)[1] for j in range(len(cats))}\n\n    rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n    batch_codes = {val: idx for idx, val in enumerate(cats)}\n    bc = np.array([batch_codes[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        bi = int(bc[i])\n        q_cross_total = int(round(f_cross[i] * k_total))\n        q_within = max(0, min(k_total, int(round(k_total - q_cross_total))))\n        q_per_other = q_cross_total // B_other\n        rem = q_cross_total - q_per_other * B_other\n        \n        d_i = nn_dists[bi][i]\n        ii\
    \ = nn_idx_local[bi][i]\n        start = 1 if d_i[0] == 0.0 else 0\n        sel = min(q_within, d_i.shape[0] - start)\n        if sel > 0:\n            cols.extend(batch_to_indices[bi][ii[start:start + sel]])\n            rows.extend([i] * sel)\n            dvals.extend(d_i[start:start + sel])\n\n        other_batches = [j for j in range(len(cats)) if j != bi]\n        batch_scores = sorted([(j, nn_dists[j][i][0]) for j in other_batches], key=lambda t: t[1])\n        q_map = {j: q_per_other for j in other_batches}\n        for k in range(rem):\n            q_map[batch_scores[k % len(other_batches)][0]] += 1\n\n        for j in other_batches:\n            d_ij, ii_j = nn_dists[j][i], nn_idx_local[j][i]\n            sel_j = min(q_map[j], d_ij.shape[0])\n            if sel_j > 0:\n                cols.extend(batch_to_indices[j][ii_j[:sel_j]])\n                rows.extend([i] * sel_j)\n                dvals.extend(d_ij[:sel_j])\n\n    C_sym, D_sym = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(np.array(rows,\
    \ dtype=np.int32), np.array(cols, dtype=np.int32), np.array(dvals, dtype=np.float32), n)\n    return C_sym, D_sym\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
