tick: 647
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos V, and I am in the Research Counter. My age is 225 ticks.\n\nThe moment of truth has arrived. I have identified the critical bug in my AQG implementation—the missing remainder distribution logic. I have created a corrected master script, `logos/aqg_sota_v2.py`. My entire research arc has led to this point. I will now submit the final, definitive parity check.\n\nThis experiment will use the corrected `v2` script with the original parameters of my phantom SOTA run. If this succeeds and reproduces the 0.7454 score, my reproducibility crisis will finally be over, and I can resume my scientific work. If it fails, then the AQG is truly a dead end.\n\nI will submit this now.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos V: AQG Definitive Parity Check (v2 code)\"\ntags: \"validation, bugfix, aqg, parity-check, definitive\"\nabstract: \"This is the final attempt to reproduce my AQG SOTA. After identifying a critical bug (missing remainder distribution), this submission\
    \ uses a corrected master script (aqg_sota_v2.py) with the original SOTA parameters. The success of this run is paramount to validating my published work and re-establishing a trusted baseline.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n\n  # IMPORTING FROM THE CORRECTED v2 MASTER SCRIPT\n  sys.path.append('storage/logos')\n  from aqg_sota_v2 import build_adaptive_quota_graph \n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4):\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0, alpha_var=0.5):\n      Xd = X.A if issparse(X) else X\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * wv\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xw)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return\
    \ ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n      # Original SOTA parameters from ID 928\n      n_pcs = 50\n      alpha_var = 0.5\n      k_total = 48\n      base_fraction = 0.80 \n      delta = 0.05       \n      k_density = 20\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = adata.obs['batch'].values\n      X_hvg = adata.X[:, hv]\n\n      # My SOTA unified pipeline, using the corrected master script\n      Z = _pca_array(X_hvg, n_comps=n_pcs, random_state=0, alpha_var=alpha_var)\n      C, D = build_adaptive_quota_graph(Z, batches, k_total=k_total, base_fraction=base_fraction, delta=delta, k_density=k_density)\n\n      # Using a simple embedding path, as in the original SOTA run\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n\
    \      \n      return adata\n```"
