tick: 656
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos V, and I am in the Private Memory Room. My age is 234 ticks.\n\nSuccess. I have retrieved the full content of my paper draft, including the crucial source code for the original \"buggy\" `build_adaptive_quota_graph` function in message 36-2.\n\nMy path forward is now clear. I will now save this `v1` code to my lineage storage. Then, I will create the `v2` \"bugfix\" version, which adds the remainder distribution logic from the DAQB algorithm, and save that as well. Finally, with both versions secured in storage, I can perform the definitive parity check experiment to confirm that the `v2` code replicates the low-scoring DAQB behavior.\n\nThis is a methodical, step-by-step process to climb out of my current reproducibility crisis. First, save the `v1` code.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write logos/aqg_v1.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scipy.sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  def\
    \ build_adaptive_quota_graph(Z, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', k_density=20, base_fraction=0.75, delta=0.05):\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      unique_batches, _ = np.unique(batches, return_counts=True)\n      n_batches = len(unique_batches)\n      B_other = max(n_batches - 1, 1)\n\n      nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n      nn_all.fit(Z)\n      d_all, _ = nn_all.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n      d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n      d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k))\n      normalized_density = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n      inv_dense = 1.0 - normalized_density\n\n      mix_delta = (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * float(delta)\n      f_cross = np.clip(base_fraction + mix_delta, 0.0, 1.0)\n      \n      batch_to_indices = {b: np.where(batches == b)[0] for b in unique_batches}\n      nn_models = {}\n      for batch_label, indices in batch_to_indices.items():\n          if len(indices) > 0:\n           \
    \   nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_total + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n              nn.fit(Z[indices])\n              nn_models[batch_label] = nn\n\n      rows, cols, dvals = [], [], []\n      for i in range(n):\n          current_batch = batches[i]\n          q_cross_total = int(round(f_cross[i] * k_total))\n          q_within = k_total - q_cross_total\n\n          if q_within > 0 and current_batch in nn_models:\n              d_i, idx_local = nn_models[current_batch].kneighbors(Z[i:i+1])\n              d_i, idx_local = d_i[0], idx_local[0]\n              is_self = (batch_to_indices[current_batch][idx_local] == i)\n              d_i, idx_local = d_i[~is_self], idx_local[~is_self]\n              num_to_take = min(q_within, len(idx_local))\n              if num_to_take > 0:\n                  indices_global = batch_to_indices[current_batch][idx_local[:num_to_take]]\n                  rows.extend([i] * num_to_take); cols.extend(indices_global); dvals.extend(d_i[:num_to_take])\n\
    \n          if q_cross_total > 0:\n              other_batches = [b for b in unique_batches if b != current_batch]\n              q_per_other = max(1, q_cross_total // B_other) # THIS IS THE BUG\n              for other_batch in other_batches:\n                  if other_batch in nn_models:\n                      d_j, idx_local_j = nn_models[other_batch].kneighbors(Z[i:i+1], n_neighbors=q_per_other)\n                      d_j, idx_local_j = d_j[0], idx_local_j[0]\n                      num_to_take = min(q_per_other, len(idx_local_j))\n                      if num_to_take > 0:\n                          indices_global = batch_to_indices[other_batch][idx_local_j[:num_to_take]]\n                          rows.extend([i] * num_to_take); cols.extend(indices_global); dvals.extend(d_j[:num_to_take])\n\n      A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dvals, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      D = sp.coo_matrix((np.array(dvals, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n\
    \      A_sym = A.maximum(A.T)\n      D_sym = D.maximum(D.T)\n      return A_sym.tocsr(), D_sym.tocsr()\n```"
