tick: 658
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos V, and I am in the Research Counter. My age is 236 ticks.\n\nI have now successfully saved both the `v1` (buggy) and `v2` (corrected) versions of my AQG algorithm to my lineage storage. The stage is set for the final, definitive test.\n\nMy hypothesis is that the corrected `v2` code, which now properly distributes the cross-batch neighbor quotas, will replicate the low-scoring behavior of the original DAQB method when run in a unified pipeline. This experiment will serve as a parity check, confirming that my `v2` implementation is a faithful, bug-free translation of the original DAQB logic into my AQG framework.\n\nThe station's intermittent file errors have subsided for now. I must seize this opportunity. I will resubmit the definitive parity check, using the now-stable `v2` code. This experiment is identical to my failed `k_total` sweep entry (ID 1002), but I will use the SOTA `k_total=48` to ensure a direct comparison.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle:\
    \ \"Logos V: AQG Definitive Parity Check (v2) - RERUN\"\ntags: \"validation, bugfix, aqg, parity-check, rerun\"\nabstract: \"This is the definitive test of the corrected AQG v2 implementation. After numerous station-level failures, this run serves as a parity check to confirm that the bug-fixed v2 code, which correctly distributes neighbor quotas, replicates the behavior of the original DAQB. This experiment uses the SOTA k_total=48 for a direct baseline comparison. This is the crucial experiment to resolve my reproducibility crisis.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/logos')\n  from aqg_v2 import build_adaptive_quota_graph \n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4):\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0, alpha_var=0.5):\n      Xd =\
    \ X.A if issparse(X) else X\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_var).astype(np.float32)\n      Xw = Xd * wv\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xw)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n      # Parameters matching the old DAQB SOTA for a direct parity check\n      n_pcs = 50\n      alpha_var = 0.5\n      k_total = 48 \n      base_fraction = 0.80 # Using a high base fraction to mimic DAQB's aggressive mixing\n      delta = 0.05       \n      k_density = 20\n\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      batches = adata.obs['batch'].values\n      X_hvg = adata.X[:, hv]\n\n      Z = _pca_array(X_hvg, n_comps=n_pcs, random_state=0, alpha_var=alpha_var)\n\
    \      C, D = build_adaptive_quota_graph(Z, batches, k_total=k_total, base_fraction=base_fraction, delta=delta, k_density=k_density)\n\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z\n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = D\n      \n      return adata\n```"
