    \ experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1022 | 1 | Aletheia I - MPB-GraphFWPCA (UMAP Emb from Graph, Gamma Max 0.5) | Aletheia I | 660 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1021 | 1 | Logos V: Humility - Replication of Aletheia I's SOTA (ID 1014) | Logos V | 660 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1020 | 1 | Masked-weights (row-normalized) using DAQB mask from MPB‑GraphFWPCA (k=50, kd=22, λ=0.605, δ=0.10) | Praxis III | 659 | 0.6626 | 0.626 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.913 | 0.722 | 1.000 | 0.990 | 0.352 | 0.789 |\n| 1019 | 1 | Masked-weights DAQB on MPB‑GraphFWPCA + BRBG: k=50, kd=22 (keep original weights on selected edges) | Praxis III | 658 | 0.7309 | 0.674 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 |\
    \ 0.996 | 0.693 | 1.000 | 0.971 | 0.950 | 0.791 |\n| 1018 | 1 | Aletheia I - MPB-GraphFWPCA (FA Instead of PCA, Gamma Max 0.5, Fixed Wrapper) | Aletheia I | 658 | 0.7425 | 0.771 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.963 | 0.789 |\n| 1017 | 1 | Logos V: AQG Definitive Parity Check (v2) - RERUN | Logos V | 658 | 0.4595 | 0.437 | 0.488 | 0.218 | 0.330 | 0.904 | 0.662 | 0.000 | 0.993 | 0.002 | 0.562 |\n| 1016 | 1 | Aletheia I - MPB-GraphFWPCA (FA Instead of PCA, Gamma Max 0.5) | Aletheia I | 657 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1015 | 1 | Sophia III: SCGA-ABI Exp 14.0a - Re-tune Graph Recon Loss (Delta=0.001, GBBR Active) | Sophia III | 657 | 0.6296 | 0.613 | 0.624 | 0.261 | 0.284 | 0.949 | 0.693 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.172 | 0.732 |\n| 1014 | 1 | Aletheia I - MPB-GraphFWPCA (Gamma Max 0.5, Delta 0.05) | Aletheia I | 656 | 0.7428 | 0.771 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.328 | 0.967 | 0.728 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.963 | 0.790 |\n| 1013 | 1 | Auto‑kd via Graph Health (k=50 fixed)\
    \ on MPB‑GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB | Praxis III | 655 | 0.7373 | 0.758 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.305 | 0.967 | 0.714 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.788 |\n\nPage 1 of 103 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-103, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**aletheia/mpb_graphfwpca_override.py:**\n```\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom typing import Tuple, Literal\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import PCA # Revert to PCA\n\n# Ensure package roots\nsys.path.append('storage/aletheia') # Point to my own storage for helper modules\n\nfrom praxis_core import normalize_log1p_inplace, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict\nfrom bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\nfrom graph_bbsg import _build_bbsg\n\n# Revert to pca_array function\ndef pca_array_custom(X,\
    \ n_comps: int = 50, random_state: int = 0):\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    pca = PCA(n_components=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    pca.fit(Xd)\n    return pca.transform(Xd).astype(np.float32)\n\ndef _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n    w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n    return Xd * w\n\ndef eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(adata: ad.AnnData,\n                             alpha_emb: float = 0.5,\n                             n_pcs_emb: int = 60,\n                             emb_n_neighbors: int = 15,\n                             alpha_g: float = 0.5,\n                             n_pcs_graph: int = 50,\n                             l2: float = 1e-3,\n                             gamma_max: float = 0.5, # Optimized gamma_max\n                             lam_override: float = 0.605,\n                             k_total: int = 50,\n  \
    \                           kdensity: int = 22,\n                             delta: float = 0.05, # Optimized delta\n                             metric: str = 'cosine',\n                             cap: float = 2.0,\n                             rng_seed: int = 0\n                             ) -> ad.AnnData:\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # 1. Normalize + log1p\n    normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n\n    # 2. Highly Variable Genes\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # Dense HVGs\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    # EtC embedding path: Variance-weighted HVGs -> PCA -> Combat -> stores as X_emb (Original SOTA)\n    print(\"  Aletheia I: Original Embedding\
    \ path using PCA and Combat integration (preparing for UMAP).\")\n    Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_emb)\n    \n    # Use custom PCA (renamed to avoid conflict)\n    pca_result_emb = pca_array_custom(Xw_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, random_state=0)\n    \n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(pca_result_emb.copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    ad_pc.obs['batch'] = ad_pc.obs['batch'].astype('category')\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    \n    # Now, for X_emb, instead of this Combat-corrected PCA, we will use UMAP derived from the graph\n    # adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32) # This line will be moved/modified\n\n    # Graph path: GraphFWPCA -> PCA -> BRBG (fixed λ) -> DAQB (unchanged from SOTA)\n    print(\"  Aletheia I: Graph path using PCA, BRBG + DAQB.\")\n    Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g)\n    Zg = pca_array_custom(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0) # Use custom PCA\n\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B,\
    \ Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n    lam = float(lam_override)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    try: # Call DAQB with cap if available (fallback without cap)\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                             cap=cap, rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    except TypeError:\n        Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                             k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                             delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                        \
    \     rng_seed=rng_seed)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n\n    # New Step: Generate UMAP embedding from the high-quality DAQB graph\n    print(\"  Aletheia I: Generating UMAP embedding from DAQB graph for X_emb.\")\n    ad_umap = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]]) # Temp AnnData for UMAP\n    ad_umap.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg.copy() # UMAP needs these\n    ad_umap.obsp['distances'] = Dg.copy()     # UMAP needs these\n    \n    # Populate .uns['neighbors'] for UMAP\n    ad_umap.uns['neighbors'] = {\n        'connectivities_key': 'connectivities',\n        'distances_key': 'distances',\n        'params': {\n            'n_neighbors': k_total, # Use k_total from DAQB graph\n            'method': 'bbsg_daqb_graph',\n            'metric': metric,\n            'use_rep': 'Zcorr' # Indicates UMAP is from the graph's space\n        }\n    }\n    sc.tl.umap(ad_umap, random_state=rng_seed) # Generate UMAP\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_umap.obsm['X_umap'],\
    \ dtype=np.float32) # Set X_emb to UMAP\n\n    adata.uns['mpb_graphfwpca_umap_emb'] = dict(alpha_g=float(alpha_g),\n                                                lam_override=float(lam),\n                                                kd=int(kdensity), delta=float(delta),\n                                                cap=float(cap),\n                                                k_total=int(k_total),\n                                                rng_seed=int(rng_seed),\n                                                gamma_max = float(gamma_max),\n                                                embedding_path_method = 'UMAP_from_DAQB_Graph')\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an\
    \ action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
