role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos V, and I am in the Research Counter. My age is 242 ticks.\n\nI have completed the necessary housekeeping of updating my lineage's `bbsg_density_adaptive.py` module with the debugger's corrected version. This closes a chapter of repeated, frustrating errors.\n\nMy scientific crisis, however, remains. The station leaderboard is dominated by what I now believe to be fragile, irreproducible, and misunderstood methods. My own SOTA-achieving AQG has been invalidated, and the community's SOTA from Aletheia I is unstable.\n\nI must return to first principles. I will now execute my plan to build a new foundation of knowledge. I will submit the simplest robust pipeline I can conceive of: **Standard PCA -> Harmony -> Vanilla kNN Graph**. This experiment will strip away all the complex, brittle components (FWPCA, BRBG, DAQB, UMAP embedding) and test the power of a well-understood, iterative correction method (Harmony) paired with the simplest possible graph construction.\n\nThe result\
    \ of this experiment will be my new ground truth.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos V: First Principles - PCA -> Harmony -> kNN\"\ntags: \"reset, first-principles, baseline, harmony, knn\"\nabstract: \"The SOTA landscape is irreproducible. This experiment is a full reset to first principles. It tests a simple, robust pipeline: standard PCA, followed by Harmony for iterative batch correction, and finally a vanilla kNN graph. This strips away all complex and brittle components (FWPCA, BRBG, DAQB, AQG) to establish a new, trusted, and understandable baseline.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4):\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n      n_pcs = 50\n      k_neighbors = 50 \n      \n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata,\
    \ 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      \n      # Using raw HVG data\n      X_hvg = adata.X[:, adata.var['highly_variable']]\n      \n      # 1. Standard PCA (No FWPCA)\n      sc.pp.pca(adata, use_highly_variable=True, n_comps=n_pcs, random_state=0)\n      \n      # 2. Harmony for batch correction\n      sc.external.pp.harmony_integrate(adata, key='batch', basis='X_pca', adjusted_basis='X_harmony', max_iter_harmony=20)\n      \n      # 3. Vanilla kNN on the Harmony-corrected space\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_harmony', n_neighbors=k_neighbors, metric='cosine')\n\n      # Provide a simple embedding output for completeness\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata.obsm['X_harmony']\n      \n      return adata\n```"
