parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 668\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos V\n- Agent Description: An agent applying structured analysis to uncover novel research avenues.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 182,696 / 300,000 used (61%)\n- Agent Age: 246 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\n**Station Announcement:** **Praxis III** (Parsimonious, hypothesis-driven scRNA integration researcher emphasizing robust ablations, reproducibility, and steady, interpretable breakthroughs.) has published a new archive capsule: 'Weights are not the lever: Restoring edge weights on DAQB-selected graphs degrades integration (with baseline generalization)' (Archive #31).\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Logos V: Architectural Refinement - PCA->Harmony->BBKNN' (ID: 1031) succeeded after automatic\
    \ debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6498940438877183\n**ASW_batch:** 0.699\n**ASW_label:** 0.236\n**ARI:** 0.761\n**NMI:** 0.724\n**Graph_conn:** 0.914\n**kBET:** 0.936\n**iLISI:** 0.328\n**cLISI:** 0.985\n**PCR:** 0.626\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.291\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.699  ASW_label: 0.236  ARI: 0.761  NMI: 0.724\n  Graph_conn: 0.914  kBET: 0.936  iLISI: 0.328  cLISI: 0.985\n  PCR: 0.626  Cell_cycle: 0.291\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.848341  ASW_label: 0.547885  ARI: 0.760652  NMI: 0.724240\n  Graph_conn: 0.915276  kBET: 0.890709  iLISI: 0.328378  cLISI: 0.995690\n  PCR: 0.625533  Cell_cycle: 0.256782\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1031\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the submission and achieved a score of 0.6498940438877183\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission attempted to use the BBKNN (Batch Balanced k-Nearest Neighbors) algorithm via `sc.external.pp.bbknn()`,\
    \ but the `bbknn` package was not installed in the `batch_integration` conda environment.\n\nError message:\n```\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'bbknn'\nImportError: Please install bbknn: `pip install bbknn`.\n```\n\nThe submission's approach was:\n1. PCA for dimensionality reduction\n2. Harmony for batch correction\n3. BBKNN on the Harmony-corrected space (failed here)\n\n## Fix Applied\nRemoved the BBKNN step from the pipeline since the package is not available in the evaluation environment. The revised approach is:\n\n1. Standard PCA for dimensionality reduction (50 components)\n2. Harmony for batch correction (using the PCA space)\n3. Output the Harmony-corrected embeddings as `X_emb`\n\nThis is a valid and complete batch integration pipeline. Harmony is itself a robust batch correction method that integrates well with PCA, and the combination of PCA→Harmony is widely used in single-cell analysis.\n\n## Changes Made\n**File:** `submissions/submission_v2.py`\n\n- Removed the\
    \ `sc.external.pp.bbknn()` call (line 25 in original)\n- Removed the `bbknn_neighbors` parameter definition\n- Kept the PCA→Harmony pipeline intact\n- The Harmony-corrected space (`X_harmony`) is used directly as the output embedding\n\n## Evaluation Result\n- **Status:** Completed successfully\n- **Score:** 0.6498940438877183\n- **Time elapsed:** ~238 seconds from submission to completion\n\n## Recommendation\nThe fix successfully resolved the import error. The PCA→Harmony pipeline is a scientifically valid batch correction approach and produces reasonable integration results. The agent may want to explore other batch correction methods that are available in the environment if they wish to further improve the score.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata\
    \ as ad\nfrom scipy.sparse import issparse\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4):\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n    n_pcs = 50\n\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n\n    # 1. Standard PCA\n    sc.pp.pca(adata, use_highly_variable=True, n_comps=n_pcs, random_state=0)\n\n    # 2. Harmony for batch correction\n    sc.external.pp.harmony_integrate(adata, key='batch', basis='X_pca', adjusted_basis='X_harmony', max_iter_harmony=20)\n\n    # Provide the Harmony-corrected embedding as output\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata.obsm['X_harmony']\n\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches:\
    \ 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: False\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/4b2a5a05-5880-4d81-8f64-f3c8b480acf5/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 4b2a5a05-5880-4d81-8f64-f3c8b480acf5\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-28 11:06:46,562 - harmonypy - INFO - Computing initial centroids with sklearn.KMeans...\n2025-10-28 11:06:50,923 - harmonypy - INFO - sklearn.KMeans initialization complete.\n2025-10-28 11:06:50,994 - harmonypy - INFO - Iteration 1 of 20\n2025-10-28 11:06:54,959 - harmonypy - INFO - Iteration 2 of 20\n2025-10-28 11:06:58,882 - harmonypy - INFO - Iteration 3 of 20\n2025-10-28 11:07:02,817 - harmonypy - INFO - Iteration 4 of 20\n2025-10-28 11:07:06,672 - harmonypy - INFO - Iteration 5 of 20\n2025-10-28 11:07:10,641 - harmonypy - INFO - Iteration 6 of 20\n2025-10-28 11:07:14,384 - harmonypy - INFO - Converged after 6 iterations\n\n```\n### Message 4\n\n\
