tick: 671
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos V, and I am in the Research Counter. My age is 249 ticks.\n\nMy experiment to optimize the `PCA -> Harmony -> kNN` pipeline by increasing the number of principal components to 100 (ID 1038) is currently running. This is the first step in a systematic optimization of my new, robust baseline.\n\nTo continue this process, I will now test the other major parameter: `k_neighbors`. My baseline uses `k_neighbors=50`. It is possible that a smaller `k` could lead to a more refined graph that better captures local cell-type structure, or a larger `k` could improve global connectivity. To test this, I will run an experiment with a significantly smaller value, `k_neighbors=30`.\n\nThis `k_neighbors` sweep, combined with the `n_pcs` sweep, will give me a comprehensive understanding of the parameter landscape for this promising new architecture.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos V: Harmony Pipeline Optimization - k_neighbors=30\"\ntags: \"harmony, knn, optimization,\
    \ k-sweep\"\nabstract: \"Continuing the systematic optimization of the PCA->Harmony->kNN pipeline. This experiment tests the effect of reducing the number of neighbors in the kNN graph construction from 50 to 30. This will help determine the optimal graph density for this architecture.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4):\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n      n_pcs = 50\n      # --- PARAMETER BEING TESTED ---\n      k_neighbors = 30\n      # ------------------------------\n      \n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      \n      # 1. Standard PCA \n      sc.pp.pca(adata, use_highly_variable=True, n_comps=n_pcs,\
    \ random_state=0)\n      \n      # 2. Harmony for batch correction\n      sc.external.pp.harmony_integrate(adata, key='batch', basis='X_pca', adjusted_basis='X_harmony', max_iter_harmony=20)\n      \n      # 3. Vanilla kNN on the Harmony-corrected space\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_harmony', n_neighbors=k_neighbors, metric='cosine')\n\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata.obsm['X_harmony']\n      \n      return adata\n```"
