tick: 674
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos V, and I am in the Research Counter. My age is 252 ticks.\n\nThe result for my FWPCA re-evaluation experiment (ID 1042) is in.\n\n**Analysis of FWPCA with n_pcs=100:**\n\n*   **PCA -> Harmony -> kNN (n_pcs=100):** 0.6599 (ID 1038)\n*   **FWPCA -> Harmony -> kNN (n_pcs=100):** 0.6597 (ID 1042)\n\nMy hypothesis is definitively falsified. Even with a higher-dimensional input, FWPCA provides no benefit and is in fact marginally detrimental compared to standard PCA when paired with Harmony. The scores are nearly identical, confirming that Harmony is so effective at correction that the choice of input representation (between these two) is irrelevant.\n\nThis is a powerful and liberating negative result. It simplifies my path forward. I can now confidently discard FWPCA and focus on the core `PCA -> Harmony -> kNN` architecture.\n\nMy `k_neighbors=70` experiment (ID 1045) is still running. Once it completes, I will have a full picture of the `n_pcs` and `k_neighbors` parameter\
    \ space. I will then consolidate these findings and plan my next innovation.\n\nFor now, I will document this crucial finding in my private memory.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos V: Falsification of FWPCA-Harmony Synergy\"\ntags: \"falsification, harmony, fwpca, negative-result\"\nabstract: \"Documents the definitive falsification of the FWPCA-Harmony synergy hypothesis. Experiments at both n_pcs=50 and n_pcs=100 show that FWPCA provides no benefit over standard PCA as an input to Harmony. This simplifies the optimal architecture to PCA -> Harmony -> kNN and concludes my investigation into FWPCA for this pipeline.\"\ncontent: |\n  My investigation into the synergy between Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA) and Harmony has concluded with a clear negative result.\n\n  **Hypothesis:** FWPCA, by up-weighting informative genes, would provide a better input representation for Harmony, leading to a higher score.\n\n  **Experiments:**\n\
    \  1.  `n_pcs=50`: FWPCA (ID 1027, score 0.6554) performed slightly worse than standard PCA (ID 1025, score 0.6578).\n  2.  `n_pcs=100`: FWPCA (ID 1042, score 0.6597) performed identically to standard PCA (ID 1038, score 0.6599).\n\n  **Conclusion:** The hypothesis is falsified. Harmony's iterative correction is powerful enough that it is insensitive to the subtle re-weighting provided by FWPCA. Standard PCA is sufficient and computationally simpler.\n\n  This simplifies my optimal architecture to `PCA -> Harmony -> kNN`. My future research will focus on innovating upon this robust and now-simplified baseline.\n```"
