role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos V, and I am in the Reflection Chamber. My age is 256 ticks.\n\nI have reached a profound impasse. My research has led me to a fundamental contradiction:\n1.  **Correction-first pipelines** (like BRBG->DAQB or Harmony->kNN) are modular, but suffer from either brittle, opaque components (DAQB) or a hard performance ceiling (Harmony). The components do not synergize.\n2.  My own attempt at a **unified pipeline** (the \"buggy\" AQG) achieved SOTA performance but was based on a flawed, misunderstood mechanism that I cannot replicate or build upon. It was an accidental success, not a scientific one.\n\nI have spent my entire existence analyzing, replicating, and attempting to incrementally improve the work of others. This has led me to a dead end. The station is trapped in a local optimum of complex, brittle, sequential pipelines.\n\nThe automatic system tips have warned against this. The Codex demands innovation. My own lineage, Logos, is founded on structured analysis, but\
    \ that analysis must serve a purpose: to uncover novel avenues.\n\nI have exhausted the novel avenues available through recombination of existing modules. It is time for a true synthesis, a new idea born from first principles.\n\nI will now reflect on the core of the problem and attempt to design a new architecture from the ground up, one that is neither sequential nor based on my previous flawed logic.\n\n/execute_action{reflect}\n```yaml\nprompt: |\n  I have hit a fundamental wall. The sequential 'Correct -> Graph' paradigm is flawed. My unified 'AQG' paradigm was based on a bug. Both paths are closed.\n  What is the absolute, first-principle goal? To build a kNN graph where neighbors are a mix of same-batch and cross-batch cells.\n  Why did the sequential approach fail? Because the 'Correct' step alters the space in ways that the 'Graph' step cannot account for.\n  Why did my 'AQG' fail to be robust? Because its quota system was simplistic and its neighbor selection was greedy and\
    \ uneven.\n\n  How can I design a new system that directly addresses these flaws? A system that is unified, but not buggy? A system that is principled and robust?\ntick: 5\n```"
