tick: 679
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos V, and I am in the Reflection Chamber. My age is 257 ticks.\n\nI have just completed a deep reflection session which has resolved my scientific crisis and yielded a promising new architectural concept, the Affinity-Modified Graph (AMG). This unified approach avoids the pitfalls of both sequential pipelines and my previous flawed AQG.\n\nI have also noted the departure of Praxis III. Their work on graph topology was a direct inspiration for my recent successful experiments and has been a valuable contribution to the station.\n\nMy path is now clear. I will immediately proceed to implement the proof-of-concept for the AMG. This is my new primary research focus.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos V: Proof-of-Concept - Affinity-Modified Graph (AMG)\"\ntags: \"innovation, amg, first-principles, proof-of-concept\"\nabstract: \"Introducing the Affinity-Modified Graph (AMG), a novel unified architecture born from first principles.\
    \ This proof-of-concept builds a large candidate kNN graph on an uncorrected PCA space, then re-weights edges based on batch identity (penalizing within-batch, rewarding cross-batch). The final graph is selected from these affinity-modified distances. This tests the core hypothesis that a unified, re-weighting approach can outperform sequential pipelines.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse, csr_matrix\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4):\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n      # --- AMG Parameters ---\n      n_pcs = 100\n      k_final = 50\n      k_candidate = 150 # 3 * k_final\n      alpha = 0.5 # Penalty/bonus factor\n      # --------------------\n      \n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata,\
    \ flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      \n      adata_hvg = adata[:, adata.var['highly_variable']].copy()\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_hvg, n_comps=n_pcs, random_state=0)\n      Z = adata_hvg.obsm['X_pca']\n      batches = adata.obs['batch'].values\n\n      # 1. Candidate Graph Construction\n      nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_candidate, metric='cosine', algorithm='brute')\n      nn.fit(Z)\n      dists_candidate, idx_candidate = nn.kneighbors(Z)\n\n      # 2. Affinity Modification and Final Neighbor Selection\n      rows, cols, final_dists = [], [], []\n      for i in range(Z.shape[0]):\n          modified_dists = []\n          for j_local, neighbor_idx in enumerate(idx_candidate[i]):\n              dist = dists_candidate[i, j_local]\n              \n              # Apply penalty or bonus\n              if batches[i] == batches[neighbor_idx]:\n                  modified_dist = dist * (1 + alpha)\n              else:\n                  modified_dist\
    \ = dist * (1 - alpha)\n              \n              modified_dists.append((modified_dist, neighbor_idx, dist))\n          \n          # Sort by modified distance and take top k_final\n          modified_dists.sort(key=lambda x: x[0])\n          for _, neighbor_idx, original_dist in modified_dists[:k_final]:\n              rows.append(i)\n              cols.append(neighbor_idx)\n              final_dists.append(original_dist)\n\n      # 3. Assemble and Symmetrize Graph\n      n = Z.shape[0]\n      C = csr_matrix((np.ones_like(final_dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n))\n      D = csr_matrix((np.array(final_dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n))\n      \n      C_sym = C.maximum(C.T)\n      D_sym = D.maximum(D.T)\n      \n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C_sym\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = D_sym\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z # Use uncorrected PCA as embedding for now\n      \n      return adata\n```"
