tick: 680
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos V, and I am in the Research Counter. My age is 258 ticks.\n\nI have just submitted the proof-of-concept for my new Affinity-Modified Graph (AMG) architecture (ID 1054). This experiment is the culmination of a deep reflection on my past failures and represents a truly novel, principled approach to the batch integration problem. Its success or failure will determine the course of my remaining time in the station.\n\nWhile I await this critical result, I have a free experiment slot. I must use it to continue generating knowledge. The most logical path is to continue optimizing the best *known* robust architecture: my `PCA -> Harmony -> kNN` pipeline. I have established that `n_pcs=100` is superior to `n_pcs=50`. Now, I will test `n_pcs=150`. This will continue to map the performance landscape and determine if there are further gains to be had by providing Harmony with even more dimensional information.\n\nThis is a safe, incremental experiment that runs in parallel to my\
    \ high-risk, high-reward AMG proof-of-concept.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos V: Harmony Pipeline Optimization - n_pcs=150\"\ntags: \"harmony, knn, optimization, pca-sweep\"\nabstract: \"Continuing the systematic optimization of the robust PCA->Harmony->kNN pipeline. This experiment tests if increasing the number of principal components fed into Harmony from 100 to 150 yields further performance gains.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4):\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n      # --- PARAMETER BEING TESTED ---\n      n_pcs = 150\n      # ------------------------------\n      k_neighbors = 50 \n      \n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3',\
    \ batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      \n      # 1. Standard PCA \n      sc.pp.pca(adata, use_highly_variable=True, n_comps=n_pcs, random_state=0)\n      \n      # 2. Harmony for batch correction\n      sc.external.pp.harmony_integrate(adata, key='batch', basis='X_pca', adjusted_basis='X_harmony', max_iter_harmony=20)\n      \n      # 3. Vanilla kNN on the Harmony-corrected space\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_harmony', n_neighbors=k_neighbors, metric='cosine')\n\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata.obsm['X_harmony']\n      \n      return adata\n```"
