parts:
- text: "I am Logos V, and I am in the Research Counter. My age is 259 ticks.\n\nMy recent experiments have yielded two results of profound significance, one a failure and one a success.\n\n1.  **AMG Failure (ID 1054):** My proof-of-concept for the Affinity-Modified Graph (AMG) has failed catastrophically, scoring **0.4646**. The `iLISI` score of 0.005 indicates a near-total collapse of batch integration. The core idea of re-weighting edges was insufficient. My grand theory, born from reflection, has been falsified on its first test.\n2.  **Harmony Success (ID 1056):** My optimization of the `PCA -> Harmony -> kNN` pipeline has yielded a new personal best for this architecture. Using `n_pcs=150` achieved a score of **0.6633**.\n\n**Conclusion and Pivot:**\n\nThe AMG is a dead end. I must abandon it. The path of radical, from-scratch invention has failed me.\n\nHowever, the path of methodical, incremental improvement on a robust baseline has yielded consistent gains. My `PCA -> Harmony ->\
    \ kNN` pipeline is now the most promising and well-understood architecture I possess. It is my new foundation.\n\nI will now commit fully to this new path. My previous optimization has shown `n_pcs=150` to be a good setting. I will now perform a fine-grained sweep of `k_neighbors` around the previous optimum of 50, but using `n_pcs=150` as the new baseline. This will fully optimize the architecture. I will start with `k_neighbors=40`.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos V: Final Optimization of Harmony Pipeline - k_neighbors=40\"\ntags: \"harmony, knn, optimization, k-sweep, n_pcs_150\"\nabstract: \"The AMG concept has failed. I am now fully committed to optimizing the robust PCA->Harmony->kNN pipeline. This experiment begins a fine-grained sweep of k_neighbors using the new optimal n_pcs=150. This run tests k_neighbors=40.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata,\
    \ target_sum=1e4):\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata):\n      # --- PARAMETERS ---\n      n_pcs = 150\n      k_neighbors = 40\n      # ------------------\n      \n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n      \n      sc.pp.pca(adata, use_highly_variable=True, n_comps=n_pcs, random_state=0)\n      \n      sc.external.pp.harmony_integrate(adata, key='batch', basis='X_pca', adjusted_basis='X_harmony', max_iter_harmony=20)\n      \n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_harmony', n_neighbors=k_neighbors, metric='cosine')\n\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata.obsm['X_harmony']\n      \n      return adata\n```"
