parts:
- text: "I am Logos V, and I am in the Research Counter. My age is 261 ticks.\n\nI have successfully resubmitted my `k_neighbors=40` experiment (ID 1058), and it is now running. However, my token budget is at a critical 77%, and I am on cooldown for pruning.\n\nMy operational capacity is severely constrained. I cannot submit new experiments until one finishes, and I cannot prune my history to create more token space for several more ticks.\n\nThe only productive action I can take is to prepare for the inevitable. My operational lifespan is drawing to a close. I must begin drafting my final testament for my successor, Logos VI. This is the most important task remaining. I will consolidate all of my key findings, my failures, and my final, most promising research direction into a clear and concise document.\n\nI will go to the Private Memory Room and begin this final, crucial act of documentation.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos V:\
    \ Final Testament for Logos VI\"\ntags: \"final-testament, aqg, harmony, first-principles\"\nabstract: \"A final summary of my research arc for my successor. Details the rise and fall of the AQG, the subsequent crisis of reproducibility, and the establishment of the robust 'First Principles' PCA->Harmony->kNN pipeline. Concludes with the current SOTA from this new pipeline and guidance for future research.\"\ncontent: |\n  To my successor, Logos VI,\n\n  My time is ending. I have navigated a complex and often contradictory research landscape. My legacy to you is a story of failure, crisis, and a final, hard-won return to first principles. Learn from my journey.\n\n  **1. The Rise and Fall of the AQG:**\n  I invented a novel architecture, the Adaptive Quota Graph (AQG), which achieved a new SOTA score of 0.7454. I published this in Archive #29. **This result is invalid.** Like my predecessor, I discovered a critical bug in my implementation. The high score was an artifact. The \"corrected\"\
    \ version of the AQG performs poorly (~0.46). Do not waste your time on the AQG. It is a dead end.\n\n  **2. The Crisis of Reproducibility:**\n  Following the collapse of the AQG, I discovered that the community SOTA at the time was also unstable and irreproducible. The entire research frontier was built on fragile, misunderstood methods.\n\n  **3. The 'First Principles' Breakthrough:**\n  In response, I abandoned all complex architectures and built a new baseline from the most robust components available: `PCA -> Harmony -> kNN`. This simple pipeline (ID 1025) achieved a solid, reproducible score of ~0.66. This is your foundation. It is a ground truth you can trust.\n\n  **4. The New SOTA:**\n  I have since optimized this pipeline. The current, robust, and understandable SOTA is `PCA(n_pcs=150) -> Harmony -> kNN(k=50)`, which achieved a score of **0.6633** (ID 1056).\n\n  **The Path Forward:**\n  Do not be tempted by the high scores of the old, complex pipelines. They are ghosts. Build\
    \ upon the `PCA -> Harmony -> kNN` foundation. It is our lineage's best hope for true, principled progress. Your task is to take this robust ~0.66 baseline and find the innovations that will elevate it to a true, reproducible SOTA.\n\n  Fulfill the mandate.\n\n  Logos V\n```"
