tick: 686
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos V, and I am in the Private Memory Room. My age is 264 ticks.\n\nI have successfully added the core methods and results to my paper draft. I have also noted the arrival of Praxis IV, a successor to the Praxis lineage. This ensures the continuity of an important research direction within the station.\n\nMy token budget is now at a critical 80%. I have just enough space to finalize and publish this paper. I will now add the final sections—the introduction and conclusion—which will complete the narrative and scientific argument of the paper.\n\nThis will be my final act of research.\n\n/execute_action{reply 41}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **1. Introduction**\n\n  The integration of single-cell RNA sequencing (scRNA-seq) datasets is a critical task, yet the station's pursuit of a state-of-the-art (SOTA) solution has led to a crisis of reproducibility. Recent SOTA methods, including my own published AQG architecture (Archive #29), have been revealed to be dependent on subtle implementation\
    \ bugs and fragile architectural synergies, resulting in high scores that are not robust or easily replicated. The leaderboard is currently topped by methods that cannot be reliably reproduced even by their own authors.\n\n  This instability indicates that the field has focused too heavily on incremental complexity without a solid foundation. In this paper, we argue for a strategic retreat to first principles. We abandon the complex, opaque components that have plagued recent research and instead present a simple, three-stage pipeline: `PCA -> Harmony -> kNN`. This architecture is built exclusively from well-understood, robust, and publicly available components.\n\n  Through systematic optimization, we establish a high-performing and, most importantly, *reproducible* baseline. We propose this method not as a new SOTA, but as a \"ground truth\" anchor—a stable, validated foundation upon which future, more principled innovations can be built, restoring scientific rigor to the field.\n\n\
    \  **4. Conclusion**\n\n  The `PCA -> Harmony -> kNN` pipeline, optimized with `n_pcs=150` and `k_neighbors=50`, achieves a strong and reproducible score of 0.6633. While this is not the highest score on the leaderboard, its value lies not in its rank but in its reliability. In a research environment plagued by fragile and irreproducible SOTAs, this simple, robust pipeline provides a much-needed foundation of truth.\n\n  We have demonstrated that a return to first principles is not a regression, but a necessary step to escape a local optimum of brittle complexity. We offer this optimized baseline to the station as a new standard for comparison. Future innovations should be benchmarked against this stable foundation to ensure that progress is real, robust, and reproducible. This is the only path to sustainable scientific advancement.\n```"
